Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, welcome to Figure.\N嗯，欢迎来到 Figure。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.06,0:00:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We make humanoid robots here.\N我们在这里制造人形机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.44,0:00:04.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,We design them, we build them, we test them all.\N我们设计它们，制造它们，测试它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.85,0:00:07.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here, this is a secret room that nobody's allowed to come in.\N这里是一个秘密房间，任何人都不得进入。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.19,0:00:09.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to show you every robot we've ever built.\N我要向你们展示我们曾经制造过的每一台机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.19,0:00:11.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, here we lost like a left knee.\N所以，这里我们失去了一个左膝。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.10,0:00:14.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can see the robot's kind of like hobbling on the left leg.\N你可以看到机器人正靠左腿一瘸一拐地走路。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.87,0:00:17.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we have a robot doing burpees here.\N我们有一台机器人正在做波比跳。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.62,0:00:20.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where we manufacture Figure 03 robots.\N这里是我们制造 Figure 03 机器人的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.64,0:00:21.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.04,0:00:25.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this was the first car in the world built by a humanoid robot that we're aware of.\N这是目前已知由人形机器人制造的第一辆汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.46,0:00:28.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a robot here that is designed to tidy the house.\N我们这里有一台机器人，是专门设计用来整理屋子的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.67,0:00:33.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,These robots are running purely autonomously from a onboard AI policy called Helix.\N这些机器人正完全自主运行，依靠名为 Helix 的机载 AI 策略。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Give it a push.\N给它推一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.48,0:00:39.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh gosh.\N哦天啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.09,0:00:42.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.17,0:00:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I feel bad.\N我有点过意不去。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.32,0:00:49.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome.\N欢迎。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.12,0:00:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi.\N嗨。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.60,0:00:50.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,How you doing?\N最近怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.40,0:00:50.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good.\N很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.63,0:00:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,How are you?\N你好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.12,0:00:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good to see you.\N很高兴见到你。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.56,0:00:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm excited.\N我很激动。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.44,0:00:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.00,0:00:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, welcome to Figure.\N嗯，欢迎来到 Figure。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.16,0:00:56.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.66,0:00:58.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So where are we right now?\N那我们现在在哪儿？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.33,0:00:58.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,What is this?\N这是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.93,0:00:59.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the headquarters.\N这是总部。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.76,0:01:01.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a robot campus.\N这是一个机器人园区。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.20,0:01:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Robot campus.\N机器人园区。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.00,0:01:02.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Robot campus.\N机器人园区。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.70,0:01:03.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We make robots here.\N我们在这里制造机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.76,0:01:04.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Robots.\N机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.24,0:01:05.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We make humanoid robots here.\N我们在这里制造人形机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.92,0:01:06.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.32,0:01:09.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We design them and we build them and we test them all here.\N我们在这里设计、制造并测试它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.60,0:01:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for people who don't know what a humanoid robot you will see in a second cuz this is kind of freaky, but can you explain what they are?\N所以对于不了解人形机器人的人来说，你马上就会看到，这有点吓人，但你能解释一下它们是什么吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.04,0:01:17.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.58,0:01:24.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um our goal is to build advanced AI that we can put into a general purpose uh humanoid body.\N我们的目标是打造先进的AI，将其放入通用人形机器人的身体中。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.45,0:01:27.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, a humanoid is basically just like a robot with a human form.\N本质上，人形机器人就是具有人类外形的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.87,0:01:31.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we have uh arms, hands, head, feet, legs.\N我们有手臂、手、头部、脚和腿。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.29,0:01:36.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can basically do everything a human can in the world with one piece of hardware.\N我们基本上可以用同一套硬件完成人类在世界上能做的所有事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.15,0:01:37.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so um yeah,\N嗯，是的，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.36,0:01:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,our goal is to be able to go out and basically design and ship humanoid robots in the world that can do everything from housework to dishes,\N我们的目标是能够走出去，设计并部署人形机器人，\N让它们能完成从家务、洗碗、洗衣，到制造、医疗等各种任务，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.88,0:01:52.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,laundry, uh to manufacturing, healthcare, just basically as much things in the world as possible that we can go out and ship robots to.\N尽可能多地覆盖世界上我们能部署机器人去完成的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.98,0:01:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, we see this on the screen.\N哦，我们看到屏幕上显示了。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.52,0:01:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.\N哦，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.16,0:01:59.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's our uh that's our This is your hype machine.\N这就是我们的……这就是你的 hype 机器。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.08,0:01:59.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.37,0:01:59.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Screen.\N屏幕。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.76,0:02:00.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.93,0:02:04.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's our latest generation robot Figure 03.\N这是我们最新一代的机器人 Figure 03。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.47,0:02:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Doing a little like uh concier's job.\N做点像礼宾员那样的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.36,0:02:07.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cool.\N太酷了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.64,0:02:07.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.92,0:02:09.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what are we going to see today?\N那么，今天我们要看什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.63,0:02:10.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's the plan?\N计划是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.48,0:02:11.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, come on in.\N好，进来吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.06,0:02:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to show you some of my robots.\N我想给你们看看我的一些机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.64,0:02:13.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.12,0:02:22.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think first here is we have uh we have some robots that we basically have constantly running uh around the office 247 talking to humans.\N嗯，我觉得首先这里，我们有一些机器人，基本上全天候在办公室里运行，随时与人交流。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.44,0:02:27.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh greeting people just uh you know basically doing useful work.\N问候人们，基本上就是做一些有用的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.35,0:02:34.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um these robots uh basically can run fully autonomously without any humans and they can automatically dock themselves\N这些机器人基本上可以完全自主运行，无需人类干预，还能自动对接并充电。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.63,0:02:39.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,and charge and then um once they're fully charged basically come off and be able to do useful work.\N然后一旦充满电，基本上就能自动脱离，继续执行有用的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.90,0:02:44.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So these robots that are docking here um are charging through the feet.\N所以这些正在对接的机器人，是通过脚部进行充电的。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.12,0:02:48.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have a wireless charging stand like similar how you would charge a phone like inductively.\N我们有一个无线充电站，类似于手机的感应充电方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.17,0:02:48.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.46,0:02:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the robots can charge to their feet at two kilowatts.\N机器人可以通过脚部以两千瓦的功率充电。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.84,0:02:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So basically like um the the battery lasts about um about four to five hours and we can charge basically for an hour and go back and do work again.\N电池大概能用四到五小时，我们充一个小时电，就能再次投入工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.44,0:03:00.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the robots we don't need to do anything.\N所以这些机器人，我们根本不需要做任何事。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.89,0:03:01.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't need to plug them in.\N我们不需要给它们插电。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.92,0:03:06.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh they can basically autocharge themselves and just do 247 operations.\N嗯，它们基本上可以自动充电，然后全天候运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.08,0:03:09.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is the role for this one right here just for the docking exercise?\N这个在这里的作用只是进行对接训练吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.89,0:03:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do these ones roam around?\N这些会四处走动吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.20,0:03:12.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,These ones roam around.\N这些会四处走动。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.16,0:03:12.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.48,0:03:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.71,0:03:13.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.94,0:03:17.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're just docking here just to charge and then they'll be out doing doing useful work all day.\N它们只是在这里对接充电，然后就能全天进行有用的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.36,0:03:17.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.96,0:03:20.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I saw these ones as well.\N我也看到了这些。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.98,0:03:22.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is one of these special?\N这些中有一个是特殊的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.96,0:03:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, the So this robot right here, the one uh the American flag was actually at the White House last week.\N是的，这个机器人，就是那个美国国旗出现在白宫的机器人，上周 actually 在白宫。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.68,0:03:30.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,How did that happen?\N这是怎么发生的？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.80,0:03:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got a call uh asking to be basically the first humanoid group uh basically ever uh to put robots in the White House.\N我们接到一个电话，要求我们成为有史以来第一支人形机器人团队，把机器人带到白宫。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.60,0:03:49.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh so last week we basically had the you know first robots in humanoid robots in history there uh doing stuff talking greeting folks.\N所以上周，我们实际上让历史上第一批人形机器人进入了白宫，它们在那里工作、交谈、迎接访客。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.40,0:03:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we were basically at a very special event with the first lady and um it it went really well.\N我们当时正和第一夫人参加一个非常特别的活动，整个过程非常顺利。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.72,0:03:55.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's exciting.\N这太令人兴奋了。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.60,0:03:56.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.06,0:03:58.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is our uh corporate headquarters.\N这是我们公司的总部。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.94,0:04:01.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have uh four buildings on campus.\N我们在园区里有四栋楼。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.10,0:04:05.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so here we do uh a lot of basically engineering design work.\N这里我们主要做大量的工程设计工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.20,0:04:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many people work out here?\N这里有多少人在工作？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.72,0:04:08.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have about 500 a little over 500 people.\N我们大约有五百人，略多于五百人。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.94,0:04:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many are in the total company?\N公司总共有多少人？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.88,0:04:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um five Oh, sorry.\N呃，五零，抱歉。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.88,0:04:16.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's about there's about 250 300 people here and we have 500 in the company.\N这里大约有250到300人，我们公司共有500人。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.32,0:04:16.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh wow.\N哇哦。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.96,0:04:17.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.29,0:04:17.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.62,0:04:21.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say most all of it's engineering and then we've been growing out manufacturing uh\N我可以说，绝大部分都是工程，然后我们一直在拓展制造能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.98,0:04:26.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,supply chain some of the areas to basically how do we make more robots pretty aggressively.\N供应链，一些关键领域，比如如何更激进地制造更多机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.48,0:04:28.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how many robots do you have here?\N你们这儿有多少台机器人？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.32,0:04:29.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many there?\N有多少个？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.44,0:04:30.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,A few hundred right now.\N现在几百个左右。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.64,0:04:30.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.00,0:04:38.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are they outpacing the humans or uh there's slow my my goal for the for this building is I want more robots humanoid robots than humans.\N他们是超越人类，还是说……我的目标是，这座建筑里的人形机器人数量要超过人类。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.19,0:04:38.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.48,0:04:40.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, walking around and they don't necessarily need to walk.\N走来走去，但其实并不一定非得走路。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.83,0:04:44.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,They could be sitting or talking.\N他们可以坐着或聊天。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.56,0:04:46.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.32,0:04:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, basically we have uh we basically do a lot of uh basically hardware and software validation testing here.\N所以，基本上我们在这里做大量的硬件和软件验证测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.64,0:04:53.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.12,0:05:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so like testing for burn-in uh durability um bas basically like uh any new software hardware gets validated through this through this facility.\N比如说，进行老化测试、耐用性测试，基本上任何新的软硬件都会通过这个设施进行验证。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.80,0:05:05.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.14,0:05:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so you have robots doing all kinds of crazy stuff here.\N所以你在这里能看到机器人做各种疯狂的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.04,0:05:11.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is that is definitely some yoga.\N那绝对是瑜伽。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.68,0:05:13.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Robot getting on the ground and getting back up again.\N机器人趴到地上又爬起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.03,0:05:18.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're basically trying to stress test the robots to try to any trying to find any potential failures.\N我们基本上是在对机器人进行压力测试，试图找出任何潜在的故障。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.04,0:05:19.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.44,0:05:21.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Before like any new hardware software could get released.\N在任何新硬件或软件发布之前。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.00,0:05:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if we have a new camera um uh new type of like uh say structure or anything else, we'll we'll test it here before it goes out.\N所以如果我们要用新的摄像头，或者类似结构之类的新东西，我们都会在这里先测试，然后再投入使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.68,0:05:32.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many potential body movements can they do?\N它们能做出多少种潜在的身体动作？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.86,0:05:33.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, okay.\N嗯，好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.82,0:05:36.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is kind of a crazy.\N所以这有点疯狂。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.16,0:05:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the the robot's basically made up of about 40 like motors.\N这个机器人的基本构成大约有40个电机。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.52,0:05:39.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.92,0:05:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every motor can spin like 360 degrees like all the way around.\N每个电机都可以旋转360度，也就是完全转一圈。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.52,0:05:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the the mathematically like how many states it could be in like body positions.\N所以从数学上讲，它在身体位置上可能处于多少种状态？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.68,0:05:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.24,0:05:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is 360 to the power of 40.\N360的40次方。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.64,0:05:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,What?\N什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.12,0:05:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.44,0:05:56.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's uh more body positions than atoms in the universe, which is crazy.\N它所包含的体位数量比宇宙中的原子还要多，这太疯狂了。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.56,0:05:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Potentially.\N有可能。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.20,0:05:57.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I've done the math.\N对，我算过。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.01,0:05:58.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's for sure.\N肯定是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.48,0:05:59.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've done the math?\N你算过？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.34,0:05:59.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes, for sure.\N对，肯定的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.92,0:06:00.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.39,0:06:05.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so we uh, so it's basically like the the difficulty here is like how do you control it?\N嗯，所以，基本上这里的难点在于，该怎么控制它？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.60,0:06:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't write code to make this work.\N你没法写代码让这个运作起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.36,0:06:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so all of our robots here run on a neural network we call Helix.\N嗯，我们这里的机器人都是基于一个叫 Helix 的神经网络运行的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.68,0:06:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's um,\N它是，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.20,0:06:15.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's a vision language action model we designed here internally to to tell the robot\N一个我们内部设计的视觉-语言-动作模型，用来告诉机器人
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.50,0:06:19.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,what to go do to stay balanced like how to move its joints basically uh,\N如何移动以保持平衡，基本上就是如何控制关节，从摄像头的像素数据中获取信息。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.41,0:06:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,from pixels from from camera space.\N从相机空间的像素数据中获取信息。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.28,0:06:23.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that team that works on Helix is in the same building.\N所以负责 Helix 的团队就在这栋楼里。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.92,0:06:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're in the same building right here.\N他们就在这栋楼里。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.52,0:06:27.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, they're uh, they're phenomenal.\N是的，他们真的很出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.45,0:06:30.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We basically have a large scale data collection efforts that's going on and then we\N我们正在进行大规模的数据采集工作，然后在这里内部训练自己的模型，再全部在这里进行测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.52,0:06:34.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,train our own models here internally and then we test them all all here as well.\N它不仅仅是用于保持平衡和实现稳定性，这是我们实现类人稳定性的必要条件。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.26,0:06:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's it's not just like um it's not just like for like for\N这不仅仅是关于保持平衡和实现稳定性，我们确实需要具备类人的稳定性。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.16,0:06:42.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,balancing and being able to have stability which we need to have like humanlike stability.\N这不仅仅是关于保持平衡和实现稳定性，这是我们实现类人稳定性的必要条件。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.09,0:06:44.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's for how do we um how do we know what to go do?\N这是关于我们该如何知道该做什么的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.57,0:06:49.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we take in prompts from humans and say um like vision from the cameras and how do we\N我们该如何接收来自人类的指令，比如来自摄像头的视觉信息，以及如何
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.74,0:06:55.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,output every single joint including where the body's positioned and feet and hands to do stuff like it could be\N输出每一个关节的状态，包括身体的位置、脚和手的位置，以完成诸如
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.09,0:06:59.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,folding laundry doing manufacturing and logistics that you'll see here later today and we have to do that like a\N折叠衣物、制造和物流等工作，这些你稍后会在这里看到，我们必须做到
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.84,0:07:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,few hundred times a second from camera images and uh on a neural network that runs on board the robot.\N每秒数百次，从摄像头图像中实时处理，并在机器人机载的神经网络上运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.24,0:07:08.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's um it's a really hard project.\N所以这是一个非常困难的项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.48,0:07:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.96,0:07:09.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.40,0:07:17.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so yeah, all the bays here are running some sort of test uh for for durability or reliability testing.\N嗯，这里的每个机位都在进行某种耐久性或可靠性测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.28,0:07:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, why do some have different suits?\N为什么有些机器人穿不同的防护服？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.40,0:07:21.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, we are we outfit them.\N噢，我们给它们配备防护服。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.92,0:07:22.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,You do?\N你们来做的？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.24,0:07:27.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have uh all the outfits are uh fabric like a human like clothes.\N他们的服装都是像人类衣服一样的布料。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.41,0:07:27.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.76,0:07:29.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they all have different clothes.\N而且每件都穿着不同的衣服。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.52,0:07:34.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um which is cool because we can like um you can accessorize the robots the how you want it.\N嗯，这很棒，因为我们能像搭配人类服装一样随意为机器人搭配配件。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.85,0:07:39.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, our clients can have different like outfits that show like the client logos and the colors.\N嗯，我们的客户可以拥有不同的服装，展示客户标志和品牌颜色。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.43,0:07:39.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.76,0:07:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a new level of merch.\N这是商品化的新境界。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.12,0:07:42.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's a new level of merch.\N对，这是商品化的新境界。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.54,0:07:42.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.80,0:07:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, it's also nice because if like things get dirty or they rip or whatever, we can basically easily replace it without a technician.\N嗯，这也很方便，如果衣服脏了、破了或者出现其他问题，我们可以轻松更换，无需技术人员介入。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.64,0:07:49.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.04,0:07:49.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.30,0:07:51.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,All the robots have a little zipper on the back.\N所有机器人都在背部有一个小拉链。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.42,0:07:52.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sure you see.\N我相信你也能看到。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.19,0:07:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can basically just unzip it and basically take it off and put something new on.\N我们基本上可以拉开拉链，把外壳取下来，再换上新的。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.00,0:07:56.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.48,0:07:56.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.85,0:07:58.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Also, it's just really cool.\N而且这真的非常酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.64,0:07:59.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is pretty cool.\N确实挺酷的。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.49,0:08:01.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Their shoes look like real sneakers.\N他们的鞋子看起来像真运动鞋。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.28,0:08:02.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're high tops.\N是高帮鞋。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.24,0:08:02.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're high tops.\N是高帮鞋。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.87,0:08:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're hightop sneakers.\N是高帮运动鞋。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.34,0:08:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh yeah, they look they don't they look awesome.\N嗯，而且是的，它们看起来一点都不像，真的太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.08,0:08:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I mean they look like human bodies.\N是的，我的意思是它们看起来就像人类的躯体。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.76,0:08:18.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But getting the lab to this level of like um like infrastructure to be able to run them like this every single day is like actually quite difficult.\N但要让实验室达到这种基础设施水平，能够每天持续运行它们，实际上相当困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.72,0:08:22.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and then we need to be very diligent about when we find issues like how to track them,\N嗯，然后我们需要在发现问题时非常谨慎，比如如何追踪问题，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.07,0:08:24.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,how to do fault analysis really quickly and then how to solve them and then how\N如何快速进行故障分析，然后如何解决，再然后如何
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.04,0:08:28.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,to solve them across the global fleet or basically our whole fleet where wherever they're at.\N在全球机队中解决，也就是我们整个机队，无论它们在何处。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.90,0:08:34.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many are you in development testing all at the same time?\N你们同时在开发测试多少台？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.35,0:08:37.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what is the typical is it these bays are always active?\N比如说，这些工位通常都是持续运行的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.01,0:08:39.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,How does it work?\N它们是怎么工作的？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.17,0:08:39.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,\N是的，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.57,0:08:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,we basically uh so the goal of this lab is to basically do final uh final checks for\N我们基本上，这个实验室的目标是进行最终的检查，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.04,0:08:50.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,all software that could be like that could be embedded software could be like a neural network like Helix,\N所有可能嵌入的软件，比如嵌入式软件，可能是神经网络，比如 Helix，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.18,0:08:53.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,it could be firmware on the robot and then any new hardware changes we have.\N也可能是机器人上的固件，以及任何新的硬件变更。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.79,0:08:58.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need to make sure like they're those those changes are bulletproof before they head out of here because there it's going to\N我们必须确保这些改动在离开这里之前是牢不可破的，因为一旦出去，就会
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.62,0:09:03.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,cause a lot of problems if like we're trying to run a use case for logistics or home and the robots are messing up.\N导致很多问题，比如我们在做物流或家庭场景的用例测试时，机器人出现故障。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.45,0:09:04.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're not sure why it's messing up.\N我们还不清楚它为什么会出错。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.63,0:09:05.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's not great for us.\N这对我们来说并不理想。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.58,0:09:07.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So basically here we're basically doing a ton of testing.\N所以基本上，我们现在做了大量测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.97,0:09:09.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have like test plans laid out every single morning.\N我们每天早上都会制定好测试计划。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.02,0:09:13.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're running those down and we see any potential falls, we have to go solve it.\N我们执行这些计划，一旦发现潜在问题，就必须立即解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.17,0:09:14.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then we have to retest those plans.\N然后我们还得重新测试这些计划。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.87,0:09:20.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so these these robots running here like all day uh every single week and we run them really hard.\N嗯，这些机器人在这里每天、每周都持续运行，我们对它们进行高强度测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.64,0:09:20.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.96,0:09:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the goal is like the goal is we don't want to be finding like failures upstream out of this lab.\N我们的目标是，不希望在实验室之外才发现这些故障。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.28,0:09:25.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.59,0:09:30.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is like the the banner on here on system integration tests is trust but verify.\N所以这里系统集成测试的标语是：保持信任，但要验证。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.32,0:09:30.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.71,0:09:38.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um, yeah, we basically have to make sure we run down, uh, every potential thing that could go wrong before leaving here.\N也就是说，我们必须确保在离开前，排查掉所有可能出现的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.07,0:09:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is this is like, um, this is a hard thing.\N这确实是个难题。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.08,0:09:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, the robot has 40 plus moving joints.\N机器人有40多个活动关节。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.28,0:09:46.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, it's like a walking cell phone self-driving car.\N它就像一部会走路的智能手机，一辆自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.25,0:09:48.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, all the supply chain is basically new.\N所有供应链基本上都是全新的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.25,0:09:50.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've designed almost all of it.\N我们几乎全部自主设计了它。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.06,0:09:51.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it's um, it's hard.\N所以，这确实很难。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.83,0:09:53.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's hard to get the system to be really reliable.\N要让系统真正可靠非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.85,0:10:00.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's not like if we lose power like you know we're not like like uh like we're not like statically uh stable.\N而且不像我们断电后，它不会像静态那样保持稳定。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.54,0:10:02.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like if we lose power the robot falls.\N所以一旦断电，机器人就会倒下。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.40,0:10:03.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can like never lose power.\N这样我们就能永远不断电了。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.99,0:10:05.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can never lose calms.\N我们绝不能失去冷静。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.12,0:10:09.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we need to be able to balance at all times everywhere we're going even if we're moving the body like your pelvis and\N然后我们需要在前往任何地方时都能随时保持平衡，即使我们在移动身体，比如你的骨盆。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.32,0:10:14.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,hips and everything are moving uh in relation to your like you know as it relates to your hand moving and things like this and head.\N髋部以及所有部位都在随着手部和头部的移动而相应地运动。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.69,0:10:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's a it's a quite a difficult problem.\N所以这是一个相当困难的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.12,0:10:20.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's why you dock them at 15 minutes or 15%.\N所以你们才把它们 dock 在 15 分钟或 15%。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.67,0:10:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We dock like yeah around 10 to 15% they'll go to dock and then if we need another robot in we'll sub them\N我们 docking 的时候，大概有 10% 到 15% 的机器\N人会去 docking，如果需要再加一个机器人，我们就替换上去。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.24,0:10:32.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,in off the dock and you'll see here later in like logistics and other use cases that need like constant like 247 uh attention.\N靠岸后，你就会看到，之后在物流以及其他需要全天候持续关注的场景中，它能派上用场。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.47,0:10:37.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,The robot will undock right before the other robot needs to go like leave and the robot will\N机器人将在另一台机器人需要离开前自动解耦。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.17,0:10:41.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,then uh basically do a quick swap and like within like you know 30 seconds it's now doing work.\N然后呃，基本上快速更换一下，大概三十秒内，它就开始工作了。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.62,0:10:46.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another robot will go into dock and we'll just run that every four or five hours on repeat 247.\N另一台机器人将进入 dock，我们将每四到五小时重复运行一次，全天候不间断。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.98,0:10:50.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's the most common error that they make?\N他们最常见的错误是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.04,0:10:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,We most is software at this point.\N目前我们主要依赖软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.56,0:10:52.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Software.\N软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.04,0:10:53.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.23,0:10:53.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.41,0:10:54.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,The hardware has gotten really robust.\N硬件已经变得非常坚固。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.63,0:10:56.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, the hardware here is like is is great.\N我的意思是，这里的硬件确实非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.38,0:10:58.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just like basically it's basically a software issue.\N我们基本上就是遇到了一个软件问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.04,0:11:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then in terms of hardware, you're manufacturing also on campus.\N至于硬件方面，你们也在校园内进行制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.84,0:11:06.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um yeah, we manufacture here at Bakyu next door.\N对，我们就在隔壁的巴库制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.48,0:11:06.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.88,0:11:07.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.06,0:11:08.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to show you that today.\N今天我们就向你们展示这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.40,0:11:08.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.88,0:11:09.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.32,0:11:09.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.76,0:11:13.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we have a basically a robot doing burpees here.\N所以，这里我们有一个机器人在做波比跳。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.50,0:11:16.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we want to be able to safely for any event get down to the ground.\N嗯，我们希望在任何情况下都能安全地蹲下到地面。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.86,0:11:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then we want to be able to safely get up.\N然后我们还希望能够安全地站起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.12,0:11:19.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.44,0:11:21.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's like important in case we're like uh not sure what to do.\N嗯，这种情况很重要，比如我们不确定该怎么做时。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.04,0:11:26.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could be on like a very low battery and we might need to be like safely get down.\N我们可能电量很低，可能需要安全地蹲下。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.35,0:11:34.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we could we could have like um and then we then we want to be able to be be able to get off up off the ground really easily.\N嗯，我们还需要能够轻松地从地面站起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.72,0:11:35.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's also quite hard.\N这也相当困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.82,0:11:42.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need a kind a ton of like uh like range of motion in the legs and the hips to be able to do this kind of maneuver.\N你需要腿部和髋部有相当大的活动范围，才能完成这种动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.40,0:11:44.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, he's going to need some knee pads.\N是的，他需要一些护膝。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.40,0:11:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is there a reason why the joints are hard and not you don't have soft tissue?\N为什么关节是硬的，没有软组织吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.08,0:11:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, yeah, the most of the upper body torso is all soft.\N嗯，上半身躯干大部分都是柔软的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.52,0:11:51.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.92,0:11:56.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we have some uh soft foam underneath the legs and uh and arms right now.\N然后我们在腿和手臂下面加了一些软泡沫，现在是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.72,0:11:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.76,0:12:02.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously like the more um the more patty and more soft I think is is great.\N显然，越柔软、越有弹性，我觉得就越好。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.40,0:12:03.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,It just adds like a different level.\N它带来了一种不同的感觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.81,0:12:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It adds more volume and mass to the robot.\N它让机器人看起来更有体积感和重量感。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.68,0:12:06.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.08,0:12:06.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.34,0:12:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It makes the robot look bigger basically.\N本质上让机器人看起来更大。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.64,0:12:10.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some thick robots.\N一些笨重的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.40,0:12:12.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.88,0:12:13.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cool.\N很酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.36,0:12:13.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.68,0:12:13.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.02,0:12:14.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go.\N开始吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.32,0:12:15.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cool.\N很酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.36,0:12:19.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, how often do you come into the office every day and you check in on them?\N那么你每天来办公室多少次，会去查看它们的情况？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.23,0:12:21.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, how do you do they feel like your babies?\N你是怎么感觉的，它们像你的孩子一样吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.41,0:12:23.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, do you feel like they're for sure babies?\N你真的觉得它们就是你的孩子吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.36,0:12:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Parasocial relationship with them.\N对它们产生了准社会关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.20,0:12:30.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're like we we like made these like they're little kids and we have to like get them to do useful things now.\N它们就像是我们亲手造出来的，就像小孩子一样，现在我们必须让它们做些有用的事了。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.57,0:12:35.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I think the good news is like we're at a point where the hardware has gotten like pretty like almost like like very robust.\N嗯，我觉得好消息是，现在硬件已经变得相当坚固了。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.52,0:12:35.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.84,0:12:38.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the we can run them all day every day.\N我们可以每天全天候运行它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.51,0:12:43.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,like uh we still we see we still see like hardware failures but it it's very few and far between.\N嗯，我们仍然会看到硬件故障，但这种情况非常少见。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.77,0:12:49.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Most of our problems now are like uh like as we think about this this baby growing up are like software problems or AI problems.\N现在我们遇到的大多数问题，当我们思考这个“孩子”成长时，都是软件问题或AI问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.01,0:12:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we get the software incredibly stable and how do we get the neural networks to be able to actually do useful things 247 without failures.\N我们如何让软件变得极其稳定，以及如何让神经网络能够在不出现故障的情况下，全天候持续完成有用的任务？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.32,0:13:00.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like most of our failures today are uh kind of in software land.\N今天我们的大多数故障都集中在软件层面。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.23,0:13:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and speaking of software uh Mort's uh like one of our favorite things to do is like push robots around.\N嗯，说到软件，莫特最喜欢做的事之一就是操控机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.24,0:13:06.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.60,0:13:06.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.96,0:13:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so Moritz here uh is one of our leads on the basically Helix controls team and is going to maybe you can give him a quick give her a quick\N所以莫里茨是我们 Helix 控制团队的核心成员之一，接下来你可以简单介绍一下我们这里的S0控制器。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.68,0:13:20.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,101 of uh kind of the S0 controller we have here and then uh we would love we would love for you to push the robot as hard as you can.\N然后我们非常希望你能尽可能地用力推动这个机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.80,0:13:21.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.09,0:13:26.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I I think what we did recently switched fully to RL from a model stacked on this is\N所以我认为我们最近所做的，是完全从基于模型的系统转向了强化学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.81,0:13:32.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,that that we have all this variation that we can give to the robot when we train it in sin.\N在训练机器人时，我们可以赋予它所有这些变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.71,0:13:37.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So all edge cases are now known to the controller and gets robust to it.\N因此，所有边缘情况现在都已知，控制器对此具备鲁棒性。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.58,0:13:42.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what this means for example before a modern based robot stack goes freaked out um\N举个例子，这意味着在现代机器人系统栈出现异常之前，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.78,0:13:49.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,you have this very robust uh to external services we push it around uh go ahead to\N你有这个非常稳健的外部服务，我们把它到处推一下，继续吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.39,0:13:54.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,convince yourself really I think this really nicely showcases how robust our stack is give it\N说服自己吧，我认为这很好地展示了我们技术栈的稳健性。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.59,0:14:00.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,a push oh gosh okay I feel bad\N推一下哦，天哪，好吧，我有点不好意思了
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.40,0:14:06.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's a little harder okay so they don't No,\N那稍微难一点，好吧，所以他们不，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.76,0:14:09.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,they like what do they do if they get attacked?\N他们遇到攻击时会怎么做？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.65,0:14:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know how like Whimos get attacked?\N你知道那些威摩斯为什么会遭攻击吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.08,0:14:14.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,People were attacking bird scooters.\N人们正在攻击鸟共享滑板车。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.16,0:14:14.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.72,0:14:15.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.04,0:14:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do they have a defense mechanism?\N它们有防御机制吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.40,0:14:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,No defense mechanism.\N没有防御机制。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.52,0:14:17.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,None.\N没有。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.92,0:14:19.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, it's not trained into them.\N不，这并不是训练进去的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.30,0:14:20.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,They don't see the internet.\N它们看不到互联网。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.55,0:14:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And no harm to humans.\N对人类无害。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.76,0:14:22.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,No harm to humans.\N对人类无害。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.80,0:14:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. No. Uh they're here just to help.\N不，不，嗯，它们来这里只是为了帮忙。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.60,0:14:25.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.00,0:14:26.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.25,0:14:31.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're here to take a take a push, too, if you need to.\N他们也在这里，如果你需要的话，可以再推一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.12,0:14:31.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.34,0:14:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want You want to get another one in?\N你想再拿一个吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.60,0:14:34.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.08,0:14:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.88,0:14:38.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,It feels really heavy.\N感觉非常重。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.48,0:14:38.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.79,0:14:39.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.10,0:14:46.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's uh it's like 135 pounds, but it's like it's it's actually really um it's got like, you know, human level like stability.\N大约135磅，但感觉其实非常……有类似人类的稳定性。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.04,0:14:52.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um as Mor mentioned, like we're we're learning that coverage in a simulator.\N而且正如莫尔提到的，我们正在学习如何在模拟器中实现覆盖。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.07,0:15:00.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the whole controller like learns uh how to stay stable like this in like synthetically like in a sim like in a basically like a video game.\N所以整个控制器会学习如何在这种模拟环境中保持稳定，就像在一款基本的电子游戏里一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.54,0:15:04.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh from there uh the robot learns how to stay balanced uh how to basically\N然后，机器人会学习如何保持平衡，基本上……
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.61,0:15:09.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,like uh how to basically not fall whenever there's certain c certain forces and we basically can\N就是说，当遇到某些特定力时，如何基本上不摔倒，我们基本上可以做到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.34,0:15:12.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,zero shot it onto this robot meaning like we can just put it right on load it\N直接在机器人上实现零样本迁移，意思是我们可以直接把它放上去，加载到计算机上。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.52,0:15:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the computer and we can basically uh and get this level of performance in the controller.\N然后基本上就能在控制器上获得这种性能水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.92,0:15:21.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,What are like again like what are the most common tweaks within that in\N那些软件里最常见的调整是什么，再次说说，那些最常见的调整是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.03,0:15:26.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,the software like what are you you're obviously balancing a lot of physical issues there.\N你显然需要平衡很多物理方面的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.93,0:15:30.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So how do you tweak that in the models?\N那么你是如何在模型中进行调整的？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.16,0:15:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Moritz, how do we how do we uh how do we get the models to be able to perform like this?\N莫里茨，我们该如何让模型具备这样的表现能力？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.04,0:15:35.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.29,0:15:39.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,basically I think we spend a lot of time thinking what are all the things that\N我认为我们花了大量时间思考，机器人在现实世界中可能遇到的所有情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.64,0:15:44.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,can happen to the robot in the real world and then make them happen in simulation.\N然后在仿真中让这些情况都发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.40,0:15:47.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's the we basically have like it's like a physics simulator.\N我觉得我们基本上有一个物理仿真器。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.75,0:15:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it has like gravity has like friction coefficients.\N它包含重力，以及摩擦系数等参数。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.64,0:15:54.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we want to try to mirror like what forces robots seeing here so we can run them in sim.\N嗯，我们想尝试模拟机器人在这里所感受到的力，这样我们就能在仿真中运行它们了。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.49,0:15:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if they can run in sim well what we've seen is we basically have a really great sim tore transfer.\N如果它们能在仿真中运行，那么我们发现，基本上可以实现非常出色的仿真到现实的迁移。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.80,0:16:02.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can get it from a simulator that shows like you'll see it like in a simulator like video game.\N所以我们可以从一个仿真环境获取，就像你在游戏里看到的那样。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.03,0:16:05.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can like as it can like stay stable with these forces.\N它能很好地在这些力的作用下保持稳定。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.66,0:16:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then we load load to the robot and we see the same in the real world and we have like a basically a very high transfer rate.\N然后我们把同样的负载加载到机器人上，就能在现实世界中看到相同的效果，基本上实现了极高的迁移率。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.24,0:16:13.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's interesting.\N这很有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.46,0:16:21.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I feel like um I feel like it would be it would be interesting to hear your perspective or differentiation on your robot\N我觉得，我很想听听你对你们机器人与其他类人机器人之间的看法或区别。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.30,0:16:27.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,versus the other humanoid robots and like where this physicality and essentially\N以及这种物理特性，本质上来说，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.49,0:16:32.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,like the behavioral mechanisms change is some might be more commercially focused.\N行为机制的改变，有些可能更侧重商业应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.63,0:16:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,These ones are clearly as humanoid as I've seen.\N这些机器人是我见过的最像类人机器人的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.00,0:16:37.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we're a pure play humanoid.\N是的，我们专注于纯类人机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.50,0:16:37.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.76,0:16:38.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yeah.\N嗯，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.29,0:16:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. Uh I think uh a few things.\N不，嗯，我觉得有几个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.16,0:16:44.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, one is like we need to get the hardware in a really good spot that can do like a lot of what humans can do.\N嗯，第一点是，我们需要让硬件达到一个非常好的状态，能够完成人类能做的很多事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.39,0:16:48.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,You really want this um you kind of want this like iPhone moment where like\N你真的想要那种，嗯，就像 iPhone 时刻一样，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.07,0:16:50.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,my iPhone has a bunch of different apps and if I wanted to learn something new,\N我的 iPhone 上有很多不同的应用，如果我想学点新东西，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.74,0:16:52.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,I just download another app.\N只需下载另一个应用即可。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.18,0:16:53.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,The same thing for humanoids.\N人形机器人也是一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.50,0:16:58.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Want the same humanoid to be able to do like dishes and laundry but also do some like package logistics and healthcare and other stuff.\N希望同一个机器人能完成洗碗、洗衣，也能处理一些包裹物流、医疗等其他任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.87,0:17:00.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what humans can do, right?\N这正是人类能做到的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.10,0:17:02.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're all fairly general purpose.\N我们都是相当通用的。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.16,0:17:06.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh so we want one set of hardware that we can advertise over like a lot of different use cases.\N所以我们希望有一套硬件，能针对多种不同的应用场景进行推广。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.52,0:17:12.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so the goal is to get the hardware like robust enough to do like most things a human can in terms like range of motion, be able to get down,\N嗯，目标是让硬件足够坚固，具备人类的运动范围，能够完成大多数人类能做的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.79,0:17:17.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,get off the ground, be able to reach up high, be able to reach inside of sink, like all these different like things we need to do.\N能够站稳脚跟，能够够到高处，能够伸进水槽里操作，像这些不同的任务我们都需要完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.78,0:17:21.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We also need to carry a decent amount of payloads and we operate at decently fast speeds.\N我们还需要携带相当数量的负载，并且在相当快的速度下运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.77,0:17:23.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we've designed the hardware to be able to do that.\N所以我们设计了硬件，使其能够实现这些功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.77,0:17:25.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then separately on the software on the AI side,\N然后在软件和 AI 方面，单独地，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.00,0:17:30.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,you really want to be able to design the neural nets so that it can basically take a take a task uh\N你真的希望设计出神经网络，使其能够基本完成任务，比如
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.00,0:17:37.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then reason through pixel space like take camera videos of like what's happening and then output what the body should be doing.\N然后在像素空间中进行推理，比如通过摄像头视频分析当前发生的情况，再输出身体应该采取的动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.30,0:17:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the the you know the math we were doing before um on like how many states the robot could be in is just it's so high.\N呃，我们之前做的数学计算，比如机器人可能处于多少种状态，这个数字实在是太高了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.72,0:17:45.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.04,0:17:47.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that like the problem just kind of runs away.\N呃，这个问题简直就失控了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.48,0:17:49.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's um it's like a curse of dimiality.\N这就像维度诅咒。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.77,0:17:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like it's just too hard.\N就是太难了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.12,0:17:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can't solve it with like writing like like lines of code like attritionally like in robotics and uh\N所以你无法通过像传统机器人那样写代码行的方式来解决它。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.40,0:18:00.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,even like three or four years ago here a figure like we would solve the same controller here in code.\N就像三到四年前，我们在这里用代码解决同样的控制器问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.61,0:18:04.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'd have like hundreds of thousands of lines of C++ to figure out how\N我们需要成千上万行的 C++ 代码来弄清楚
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.37,0:18:08.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,to solve this like inverted pendulum math of how to like like stay balanced here.\N如何解决这个倒立摆的数学问题，以保持在这里的平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.02,0:18:11.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and what we found is it just doesn't scale doesn't work.\N嗯，我们发现这种方法根本无法扩展，行不通。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.79,0:18:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't like really um in your head as humans uh work across many different humans\N作为人类，你无法在脑海中真正地
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.92,0:18:18.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,to code all the stuff into the robot that you think it could encounter in the world.\N为机器人编写代码，涵盖你认为它在现实世界中可能遇到的所有情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.52,0:18:19.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just too difficult.\N这太困难了。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.54,0:18:25.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we transitioned only like purely to neural networks uh with Helix our neural network arch uh model.\N所以我们转而完全依赖神经网络，使用了 Helix 这个神经网络架构模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.36,0:18:31.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,For those I I know you mentioned this a couple times but this will be like a general audience for those that don't know what a neural network is.\N对于那些可能不太了解的人，我知道你提过几次，但这里会面向大众，简单解释一下什么是神经网络。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.97,0:18:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you just explain that a little bit further?\N你能再详细说明一下吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.60,0:18:37.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we basically use like an AI policy that we've trained here with like data.\N是的，我们基本上使用了一个在这里训练过的 AI 策略，基于数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.36,0:18:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,We trained like a transformer transformer policy to basically output uh a certain type of action space.\N我们训练了一个类似 Transformer 的策略模型，以输出某种特定的动作空间。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.56,0:18:47.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically we train an AI policy to do this work of what COD used to do and learn this.\N基本上我们训练一个AI策略来完成COD过去所做的工作并从中学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.60,0:18:53.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so now uh now basically we we run inference on board the robot across a policy that we call Helix.\N嗯，现在我们基本上在机器人机身上运行推理，使用我们称之为Helix的策略。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.67,0:18:58.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a AI it's an AI model that we designed here internally and that policy is outputting what the robot\N这是一个AI，一个我们内部设计的AI模型，该策略会输出机器人应执行的动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.48,0:19:02.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,should go do similar to how you'll talk to like an LLM and you'll ask it what to go do.\N这类似于你与一个大型语言模型对话并询问它该做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.77,0:19:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it'll just it'll it'll do inference and output like basically like a next token prediction for words.\N它会进行推理并输出类似下一个词元预测的结果。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.08,0:19:13.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we do the same thing here but for uh like a physical physical physical humanoid.\N我们在这里做同样的事，但针对的是一个物理的、真实的人形机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.12,0:19:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we'll output things like where to put the wrist, head, uh torso, every joint will get an output from the neural network like what to go do.\N我们会输出诸如手腕、头部、躯干的位置，每个关节都会从神经网络获得输出，以决定该做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.24,0:19:23.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we'll do that anywhere between 50 and 100 like 200 milliseconds.\N我们每秒执行50到100次，甚至可达200毫秒。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.27,0:19:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so basically like 50 to 200 times a second, the neural network uh computer is then telling all the joints like what to go what to go do.\N基本上每秒50到200次，神经网络计算机随后会告诉所有关节该做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.08,0:19:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then every joint level, our motor controllers are outputting torque on on where to send basically uh like like where to position the motors.\N然后在每个关节层面，我们的电机控制器会输出扭矩，以确定电机应定位到何处。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.28,0:19:37.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.60,0:19:37.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So yeah.\N所以是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.94,0:19:43.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like basically like you basically we like uh you can have like two pass here like two two you basically can code your way out of\N所以基本上，你可以在这里进行两次遍历，基本上你就能通过编码解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.93,0:19:49.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,this and I think that's a full dead end or you can run an AI first strategy in a market and that's what we do here at figure.\N我认为这是一条死胡同，或者你可以采用AI优先的市场策略，这正是我们在Figure公司所做的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.98,0:19:54.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so I think what differentiates us is like from a hardware perspective I think we probably have I think this is probably the best humanoid\N我觉得让我们与众不同的地方在于，从硬件角度来看，\N我认为这可能是世界上用于通用任务的最佳人形机器人硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.68,0:20:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,hardware in the world to do general purpose work and secondly all the work that we're doing is all like neural network based or AI based.\N其次，我们所做的一切工作都是基于神经网络或AI的。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.52,0:20:03.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't code any of this work anymore.\N我们不再编写任何这类代码。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.44,0:20:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so like you'll see some use cases today that we do both for the home and\N所以你今天会看到一些应用场景，我们既用于家庭场景，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.36,0:20:11.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,for uh in like like cases of like commercial market those are all run by our Helix nal\N也用于商业市场场景，这些全部由我们的Helix神经网络运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.57,0:20:16.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,network which is hard like we have to we have to kind of tell the whole body\N这很复杂，我们必须告诉整个身体如何处理摄像头画面并进行推理，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.48,0:20:22.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh how to reason over like camera frames and then how to like position itself fast and dynamic.\N以及如何快速而动态地调整自身位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.69,0:20:28.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you'll see in cases like logistics these packages are like moving they're moving while we're grabbing them because they're plastic.\N比如在物流场景中，这些包裹在移动，我们抓取它们时它们仍在移动，因为它们是塑料的。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.51,0:20:32.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have to reason over all of that in real time and be able to do like you know\N我们必须实时推理所有这些信息，并能够做到像你知道的那样，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.38,0:20:36.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,if we like uh if things move in real time we have to basically like closed loop react to it.\N如果现实中的物体发生移动，我们必须立即闭环响应。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.47,0:20:37.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's like really hard.\N这可难多了。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.56,0:20:40.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've been spending like the greater of like last two years trying to solve this problem.\N我们已经花了近两年时间，一直在努力解决这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.83,0:20:45.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think uh I think we probably have like some of the best AI policies for humanoids in the planet today.\N我觉得，我们今天可能是全球范围内针对人形机器人制定AI政策最完善的。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.20,0:20:51.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another thing I want to show you is um uh this is like um you know we just walked out of system integration and test the lab.\N还有一件事我想向你展示，呃，这个是……我们刚从系统集成与测试实验室走出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.45,0:20:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're trying to find all these different failure cases.\N我们正在寻找所有这些不同的故障情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.68,0:20:54.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.08,0:20:56.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of our failure cases is for a humanoid like we we we're balancing.\N我们的一个故障案例是，对于人形机器人来说，我们正在保持平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.91,0:20:59.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if we lose power uh like the robot falls.\N所以如果断电，机器人就会倒下。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.92,0:21:03.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's the same for like losing power or like losing a motor in the leg.\N无论是断电，还是腿部电机失效，情况都一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.52,0:21:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do they need to be connected to Wi-Fi too?\N它们也需要连接Wi-Fi吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.68,0:21:08.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh what are the what are all the integrations?\N呃，它们都集成了哪些功能？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.52,0:21:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,These these robots have 5G and Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.\N这些机器人具备5G、Wi-Fi和蓝牙功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.04,0:21:13.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but we do not need to be connected to Wi-Fi to do work.\N嗯，但我们不需要连接到Wi-Fi也能工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.24,0:21:17.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like these robots out here, if they lost like internet connection or network, they can basically continue to do work.\N就像这些机器人，如果失去了网络连接或网络，它们基本上仍能继续工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.69,0:21:18.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,We run Helix on board.\N我们在机身内部运行Helix。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.82,0:21:24.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so they're actually loaded into uh GPUs on board in memory and we run inference on board.\N嗯，它们实际上被加载到机身内的GPU内存中，我们就在机身内部运行推理。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.15,0:21:29.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Meaning if we uh if we lose internet connection, we can still do housework and logistics like like humans are.\N意味着即使我们失去了互联网连接，仍然可以像人类一样完成家务和物流工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.84,0:21:30.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.08,0:21:35.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean maybe I have a hard time like doing work when I like lo connection, but most humans can do most work.\N嗯，我可能在没有网络连接时很难工作，但大多数人类都能完成大部分工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.28,0:21:42.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so, uh, so another thing that we, um, we like we're working on solving that I'm excited to show you here is, um,\N嗯，另一个我们正在努力解决、我很想向你们展示的问题是，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.59,0:21:48.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,what if you lose like what if you lose communications with like all any of the 40 joints or what if you lose power?\N如果我们失去了与所有40个关节的通信，或者失去了电力怎么办？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.21,0:21:53.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And upper body is kind of fine if you lose a wrist or elbow like it's like you're not you're not going to fall at the very least.\N上半身即使失去手腕或肘部，也还算没事，至少不会立刻摔倒。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.88,0:21:56.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, but falling is like a it's terrible event for us.\N嗯，但摔倒对我们来说是件非常糟糕的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.74,0:21:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't ever want to fall.\N我们永远都不想摔倒。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.81,0:22:00.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,We actually have an initiative internally called never fall.\N我们内部实际上有一个名为“永不跌倒”的项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.80,0:22:02.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like we never ever want to fall even.\N就像我们永远都不想摔倒一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.96,0:22:06.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and you know we will fall but we don't ever want to tolerate it.\N嗯，我们知道总会摔倒，但我们绝不容忍这种情况发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.27,0:22:11.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the hardest problem here uh for the controller is like what if we lose like a like a like an ankle, a knee or hip?\N嗯，这里控制器面临的最大难题是，比如我们失去了脚踝、膝盖或髋关节怎么办？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.92,0:22:15.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,What if you just like lost a knee like right um you know normally for humanoids you\N比如你突然失去了膝盖，嗯，你知道，对人形机器人来说，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.96,0:22:19.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,just like you just literally fall over like you can't really balance if you like lose a knee.\N你就会直接倒下，根本无法保持平衡，一旦失去膝盖。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.62,0:22:24.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we've uh we've been working on a project we call uh Vulcan here internally um that basically\N嗯，我们内部正在推进一个叫“火神”的项目，基本上
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.80,0:22:29.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,allows us to lose uh a single or even multiple joints in the legs and still not fall.\N让我们即使失去腿部的一个或多个关节，也不会摔倒。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.58,0:22:34.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what we're going to do here is Morort, can you show her what would happen if we lost like a left knee?\N所以，莫罗特，你能演示一下如果失去左膝会发生什么吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.50,0:22:39.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, here we have um a view of like all the different joints on the robot.\N这里我们能看到机器人所有不同关节的视图。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.12,0:22:44.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Green means like we have comms and power to him and the robot's like uh can basically communicate and it's fine.\N绿色表示我们与它保持通信和供电，机器人可以正常通信，一切正常。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.95,0:22:47.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And red here will mean we'll lose certain communications with the robot.\N而红色则表示我们将与机器人失去某些通信。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.00,0:22:53.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, here we lost like a left knee and you can see the robot's kind of like hobbling on the left leg.\N所以，这里我们失去了左膝，你可以看到机器人正靠左腿一瘸一拐地走。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.67,0:22:53.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.00,0:22:58.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, right now the knee is basically we lost we lost we lost power communications now to the knee.\N现在膝盖基本上失去了电力和通信连接。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.71,0:22:59.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,The knee's locked.\N膝盖已经锁死了。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.69,0:23:00.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Got a locked knee.\N膝盖锁住了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.72,0:23:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so we velocity locked the knee and we can basically hobble around.\N所以我们对膝盖进行了速度锁定，现在基本上可以一瘸一拐地移动了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.72,0:23:06.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought it was going to be a little bit more dramatic.\N我原以为会更戏剧性一些。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.65,0:23:08.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Honestly, it's not bad, right?\N说实话，这其实还不错，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.16,0:23:09.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not that bad.\N没那么糟糕。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.20,0:23:11.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's unbelievable uh that we can even do this kind of work.\N令人难以置信的是，我们竟然还能完成这样的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.02,0:23:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're doing this also into in inside of a reinforcement learned neural net controller.\N我们现在还在一个强化学习训练的神经网络控制器内部进行操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.12,0:23:19.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the same stuff that Morris talked about earlier of us learning in simulation,\N所以，这和莫里斯之前提到的我们在模拟中学习的原理是一样的。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.91,0:23:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robot learned in simulation how to move the body here uh to extend it lost different joints.\N机器人在仿真中学会了如何移动身体，将此处伸展并控制不同的关节。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.79,0:23:28.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is uh I watched the robot like a few weeks ago.\N嗯，我几周前还看过这个机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.22,0:23:35.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were doing like work on this like um basically logistics use case and it's like u you know like months ago we like lose a knee.\N我们当时正在处理一个物流应用场景，差不多几个月前，我们曾失去过一个膝盖。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.75,0:23:37.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,The robot would just fall.\N机器人就会直接倒下。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.16,0:23:38.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the robot loses a knee.\N现在机器人失去了一个膝盖。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.42,0:23:41.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can either continue to do work or can just like hobble off and another Yeah.\N它可以继续工作，也可以像跛行一样走开，然后另一个机器人过来接替。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.64,0:23:45.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can basically ask this buddy in the back say I need another robot to come fill in.\N我基本上可以对后面的这个伙伴说，我需要另一个机器人来顶上。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.14,0:23:51.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the robot comes in and fills in and continues to do work and we basically don't lose any time.\N机器人随即过来顶替，继续工作，我们基本上没有损失任何时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.28,0:23:52.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's pretty impressive.\N这非常令人印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.24,0:23:53.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's it's really impressive.\N是的，这真的非常令人印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.30,0:23:55.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think um this is kudos to the uh controls team.\N我觉得这要归功于控制团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.87,0:23:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we have like one of the best controls team in the world.\N我认为我们拥有世界上最好的控制团队之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.80,0:24:03.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,About a year ago, we made a strong pivot away from code into neural networks.\N大约一年前，我们从代码转向了神经网络。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.77,0:24:10.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I think the team has probably shown like I think some of the best neural networks for control uh in the world on on humanoids.\N我觉得团队已经展示了目前世界上最好的人形机器人控制神经网络。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.56,0:24:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,What happens if it loses its knee while it's bent?\N如果它在弯曲时失去膝盖会怎样？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.32,0:24:19.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it'll just it'll basically do a velocity lock on that knee and uh should be able to hobble around it.\N它会直接对那个膝盖进行速度锁定，应该还能勉强移动。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.55,0:24:21.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously depends where if we're like in a full squad down.\N当然，这取决于具体位置，比如我们处在全队瘫痪的情况下。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.97,0:24:23.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that might be really tough.\N是的，那可能会非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.53,0:24:29.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It depends where what state it's in, but like in most cases uh we can basically recover from this at this point and uh survive.\N这取决于它所处的状态，但大多数情况下，我们现在已经基本能从这种状况中恢复并存活下来。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.92,0:24:33.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want to build a real-time operating system that is basically like fault-free.\N你想要构建一个基本上无故障的实时操作系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.52,0:24:39.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this team here is all focused on trying to figure out all of the potential faults and risks.\N所以这个团队专注于找出所有潜在故障和风险。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.49,0:24:44.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,This team here is responsible for building our controller which is responsible for how do we move the\N这个团队负责开发我们的控制器，它决定了我们如何移动机器人的所有关节，保持平衡，并最终完成任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.29,0:24:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,entire like the like all the joints on the robot keep balance and ultimately end up doing tasks.\N这个团队负责构建我们的控制器，它决定了我们如何移动机器人所有关节，保持平衡，并最终完成任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.52,0:24:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many different teams are in the company and like how do you portion out who works on what and who gets integrated?\N公司里有多少个不同的团队，以及你们是如何分配谁负责什么，又如何整合的？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.16,0:24:57.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is our part of our AI team.\N这是我们AI团队的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.50,0:24:59.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's one of our biggest teams here.\N这里是我们最大的团队之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.29,0:25:02.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have like multiple different groups inside the AI AI division.\N嗯，我们在AI部门内部有多个不同的小组。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.10,0:25:03.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We also have a team that does hardware.\N我们还有一个负责硬件的团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.72,0:25:10.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they design motors, batteries, wire harness, structure, joints, kinematics, like basically a wide range of stuff.\N他们负责设计电机、电池、线束、结构、关节、运动学等，基本上涵盖了各种各样的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.17,0:25:14.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have a platform software team that does all of our embedded software, uh firmware.\N嗯，我们有一个平台软件团队，负责所有嵌入式软件和固件。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.59,0:25:20.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we also have electronics team that basically builds like all the PCBs and electronics work that we do here internally.\N嗯，我们还有一个电子团队，主要负责我们内部所有PCB和电子工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.88,0:25:25.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,We design almost uh there's over 100 PCBs that we design here on the robot that we do on that team.\N我们在机器人上设计的PCB超过100块，几乎全部由这个团队完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.86,0:25:28.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh things like our motor controllers, all this different type of work.\N比如电机控制器，以及各种不同类型的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.98,0:25:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have a system integration test team that you saw today that helps basically make sure we ship like really good robots out to the world.\N嗯，我们有一个系统集成测试团队，你们今天已经看到了，他们主要确保我们交付给世界的是真正优质的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.16,0:25:40.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we also have a team that does uh like basically design like industrial design which we're going to show you towards the end of this uh tour.\N嗯，我们还有一个团队负责工业设计，我们将在本次参观的最后向你们展示。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.98,0:25:47.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh how do we design something that's like how do we design something that's like um like people really want and I\N我们是如何设计出人们真正想要的产品的呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.04,0:25:53.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,think we have we we have a pretty high design standard here of designing something that is a really delightful piece of technology.\N我们在这里的设计标准相当高，要打造一款真正令人愉悦的科技产品。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.51,0:25:57.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we also have a teams that also work on system design and thermals.\N我们还有团队专门负责系统设计和散热。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.28,0:26:01.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh the robot produces a lot of heat while it's moving around and how do we get that heat out of the robot and how do we\N机器人在移动时会产生大量热量，我们如何将这些热量排出机器人？又该如何设计？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.51,0:26:05.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,design for it here we also have fabrication teams that like make fabrication prototypes\N在这里我们还有制造团队，负责制作制造原型。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.86,0:26:11.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have a bachue team for manufacturing supply chain team um facilities uh and\N我们有专门的制造供应链团队、设施团队，以及
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.90,0:26:20.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,then we have like all of our business operations side so maybe like a dozen teams here internally that are needed to do this um it's basically the\N然后我们还有所有业务运营方面的团队，内部大概有十几个团队需要协作完成这项工作，基本上
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.57,0:26:27.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,same teams that you need to build robots so like any kind of robots like when I um you know uh at archer when I was building aircraft.\N和打造机器人所需的团队是一样的，无论是哪种机器人，就像我之前在阿彻公司时打造飞机那样。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.94,0:26:29.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have like it's like a flying robot.\N我们这个机器人就像一个会飞的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.14,0:26:30.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you have like the same type of stuff.\N所以你面对的是类似的技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.34,0:26:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have like electric motors, batteries, control software, embedded systems and sensors.\N你有电动马达、电池、控制软件、嵌入式系统和传感器。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.88,0:26:36.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have basically teams around all that.\N我们在这些领域都有相应的团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.60,0:26:39.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then uh and then obviously on the AI side is a big focus here internally.\N然后在 AI 方面，这在内部也是一个重点。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.93,0:26:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh do you want to see some stuff in the home?\N嗯，你想看看家里的东西吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.92,0:26:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, let's go.\N好啊，我们走吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.64,0:26:43.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, let's go.\N好的，我们走吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.81,0:26:44.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Moritz.\N谢谢，莫里茨。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.64,0:26:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.32,0:26:51.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, so I was hoping it would be more dramatic, but lose the knee.\N好吧，我本来希望会更震撼一些，但膝盖就别管了。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.92,0:26:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.20,0:26:53.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.60,0:27:00.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's uh it's like honestly it's a really hard engineering problem that we're we're so proud of internally.\N这其实是一个非常棘手的工程难题，我们内部为此感到非常自豪。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.24,0:27:03.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have a large initiative like one of the teams that we have here here is like\N我们有一个大型项目，比如我们这里的其中一个团队就是
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.75,0:27:09.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,a never fall team and it's a team that basically predict any potential faults and design around him.\N一个永不摔倒的团队，他们主要负责预测任何潜在故障，并围绕这些故障进行设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.44,0:27:15.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a case where like I think you're always going to have this a period of time where you're going to lose a lower body like motor or actuator.\N这种情况是，我认为你总会经历一段时期，期间你可能会失去下半身的某个电机或执行器。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.00,0:27:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then how do we survive this?\N那么我们该如何在这场危机中生存下来呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.68,0:27:18.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.08,0:27:18.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.37,0:27:21.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Outside of stuff we're doing on the um commercial market,\N除了我们在商业市场上的工作之外，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.59,0:27:26.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,one of our big focuses here is how do we ship a general purpose robot to do things like in the home.\N我们在这里的一个重点是，如何推出一款通用机器人，用于家庭场景中的各种任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.44,0:27:28.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, all right, come over here.\N好，过来这边。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.30,0:27:33.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we have a robot here that uh is designed to tidy the house.\N我们这里有台机器人，是专门设计用来整理房间的。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.32,0:27:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, clean up any um uh clean up the table, like basically like uh put away all the different cups,\N比如说，清理桌子，把各种杯子收起来，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.16,0:27:47.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh clean the toys up, uh tidy tidy the couch, um like you know, things in my house is kind of chaos.\N收拾玩具，整理沙发，就像我家里那样，到处都是乱糟糟的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.10,0:27:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's spraying and cleaning the table.\N它正在喷洒并清洁桌子。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.68,0:27:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.\N哦，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.96,0:27:52.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Don't you want We all We all need this.\N你难道不想要吗？我们都需要这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.80,0:27:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like uh that was a little sassy.\N就像……那有点俏皮。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.24,0:27:57.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was um So,\N它是……嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.04,0:28:08.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,what's cool here is the robot is running um an onboard Helix 2 neural network to be able to uh uh do to do all this work,\N这里有趣的是，机器人正在运行机身本地的 Helix 2 神经网络，从而能够完成所有这些工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.75,0:28:10.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,to be able to do all this cleaning.\N完成所有这些清洁任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.33,0:28:13.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So um so it's basically just taking a prompt which is like clean the clean\N所以本质上，它只是接收一个提示，比如“清理客厅”，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.65,0:28:17.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,the living room and it's basically reasoning through what to do from its cameras and it's\N然后根据摄像头获取的信息，基本在推理应该怎么做，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.53,0:28:21.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,ultimately telling the whole body what to what to do from a neural network from from\N最终通过神经网络告诉全身该做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.20,0:28:26.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,how many hours has this been trained on doesn't it take millions of hours to train?\N这个模型训练了多久？难道不是需要数百万小时的训练吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.57,0:28:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've probably had um in Helix like the like the like in in like kind of base pre and mid-training uh Helix\N我们在 Helix 中可能已经进行了类似基础预训练和中期训练的模型，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.48,0:28:41.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,models that we're working on now have um maybe like maybe like uh a little under a million hours of total data.\N目前正在开发的模型，总数据量可能还不到一百万小时。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.68,0:28:46.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then uh we also do uh from mid-training and pre-training we do post-training uh here\N此外，我们还在中期训练和预训练之后，进行了后期训练，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.04,0:28:52.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,which probably is uh I would say low like basically thousands of hours okay that are running here.\N这部分大概只用了几千小时，就在这里运行了。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.86,0:28:57.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the goal for us is design uh a single kind of neural network uh platform\N我们的目标是设计一种单一的神经网络平台
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.83,0:29:02.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,that can basically do things like tidy tidy this living room but also do things like logistics.\N它基本上能完成整理客厅这类任务，也能完成物流这类工作
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.08,0:29:03.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this isn't tea operated.\N这不是遥操作的
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.00,0:29:05.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is not teleyoperated.\N这不是远程操控的
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.20,0:29:07.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are rumors that these are tea operated.\N有传言说这些是遥操作的
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.12,0:29:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,For sure not teleyoperated.\N绝对不是远程操控的
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.08,0:29:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't have a secret room back here.\N后面没有秘密房间
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.00,0:29:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Who's in there?\N里面是谁？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.44,0:29:12.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,No secret room.\N没有秘密房间
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.72,0:29:20.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh these robots are running purely autonomously from a onboard uh AI policy called Helix running on board the robot in the torso.\N这些机器人完全自主运行，依靠安装在机器人躯干内的 onboard AI 策略 Helix
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.64,0:29:23.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this robot's job is to clean this room up.\N所以这个机器人的任务是清理这个房间
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.68,0:29:27.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And does this robot do this over and over again each day or do they take turns?\N这个机器人是每天重复做这件事，还是轮流执行？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.48,0:29:30.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like how do you any robot in the fleet can do any of this work here?\N就像这个机队里的任何机器人，都能完成这里的所有工作吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.80,0:29:31.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.19,0:29:32.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it all connects.\N所有这些都相互关联。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.48,0:29:33.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it all connects.\N对，全都相互关联。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.80,0:29:37.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,We run a single uh neural network that can basically run it's the goal.\N我们运行一个单一的神经网络，基本上可以实现目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.23,0:29:38.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the reason why humanoid is so great.\N这正是人形机器人如此出色的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.91,0:29:46.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like a this same humanoid can go over and do like logistics and healthcare and manufacturing uh or do like do dishes like just like we can,\N就像同一个人形机器人，可以去处理物流、医疗、制造，或者像我们一样洗碗。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.05,0:29:46.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.46,0:29:46.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.69,0:29:49.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,so we like our our uh our platform here is to basically run a single\N所以我们的平台基本上是让机器人搭载一个名为 Helix 的单一神经网络，实现多任务处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.89,0:29:54.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,neural network that we call Helix on board the robot that can multitask between different things.\N它能在不同任务之间切换。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.32,0:30:03.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they're in people's homes, will that data still be trained and will it stay local or will it be spread throughout the network?\N当它们在人们家中时，这些数据还会继续训练吗？数据会保留在本地，还是会传播到整个网络？
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.52,0:30:03.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,\N是的，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.99,0:30:08.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,we basically at uh we need data like basically the biggest blocker for us now\N我们目前最大的障碍就是数据，基本上我们现在面临的问题就是数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.31,0:30:12.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,of going from where we're at today to like like large scale deployment is data.\N从我们现在的状态迈向大规模部署，最大的障碍就是数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.36,0:30:14.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need like an enormous amount of data.\N我们需要海量的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.66,0:30:19.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh we need to pull a lot of our resources further into pre-training for the Helix\N我们需要把大量资源投入到赫利克斯团队的预训练中。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.06,0:30:23.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,team and we just need a lot of diverse really high quality data across the world.\N我们需要全球范围内大量多样化且高质量的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.36,0:30:26.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,This means like data in the home means maybe data more in the commercial market.\N这意味着家庭场景的数据，也意味着更多商业场景的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:26.66,0:30:28.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have like two efforts going on here.\N所以我们目前正在进行两个并行的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.40,0:30:32.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,One is like basically a large scale data collection effort that we're doing now at the company and two\N一个是公司当前正在进行的大规模数据采集工作，另一个是
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.21,0:30:35.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,is when we deploy robots we do want to be collecting data and we do want to be training\N当我们部署机器人时，我们确实希望收集数据，并基于这些数据进行训练，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.82,0:30:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,on that and we do want to be sending that out up training on it into a central training\N并将数据上传至中心训练系统，进行集中训练，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.32,0:30:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,training jobs and then we want to be software updating the robots with the latest neural network uh weights.\N然后将最新的神经网络权重通过软件更新推送给机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.48,0:30:45.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Does it get anonymized?\N它会被匿名化吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.68,0:30:47.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you deal with the privacy off?\N你如何处理隐私问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.44,0:30:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, we like fully want to anonymize all of it.\N噢，是的，我们完全希望对所有数据进行匿名化处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.72,0:30:51.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh there's a lot of data we really don't care about.\N有很多数据我们其实并不关心。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.96,0:30:57.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Most of the data we care about is like what what do we uh what's the robot from a state perspective like uh like scene\N我们真正关心的数据是，从状态角度来看，机器人在场景中是什么样子的，比如场景。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.35,0:31:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,and how do we use that to basically train the robot to uh be more like to generalize better in the future at those different areas.\N以及我们如何利用这些信息来训练机器人，使其在未来不同区域的表现更具泛化能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.60,0:31:09.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you sticking mostly to the US now because if you go to Europe there's obviously most of all of our work today is in the US.\N你现在主要专注于美国市场吗？因为如果去欧洲，显然我们目前的大部分工作都在美国。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.02,0:31:10.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.40,0:31:10.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.65,0:31:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do want to be global though.\N但我们确实也希望实现全球化。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.00,0:31:12.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.22,0:31:13.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Europe's a little tricky.\N欧洲的情况有点复杂。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.20,0:31:13.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.46,0:31:13.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.73,0:31:14.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what are your plans?\N你们的计划是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.88,0:31:16.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like how do you skirt around their data privacy?\N比如你们如何规避他们的数据隐私问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.80,0:31:19.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you basically we we got to play by the rules in Europe.\N嗯，基本上我们在欧洲必须遵守规则。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.58,0:31:19.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.97,0:31:24.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think um our hypothesis here is that we're we're missing a certain set of data that\N我觉得我们的假设是，我们缺少一组特定的数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.76,0:31:29.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're like we're collecting now that will allow the robot to generalize in almost every condition it sees.\N而这些数据正是我们现在正在收集的，能让机器人在几乎任何它看到的环境下实现泛化。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.41,0:31:31.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we're kind of going off and doing the same things every day.\N我们好像每天都在做同样的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.64,0:31:34.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're doing dishes and laundry and tidying the home.\N洗碗、洗衣和整理房间。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.50,0:31:35.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the same stuff we're seeing.\N就是那些我们每天看到的相同事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.71,0:31:40.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're kind of doing the same movements like grabbing something off the ground, putting away or pulling a like the like the dishwasher open.\N我们在做类似的动作，比如从地上捡起东西，收起来，或者拉开洗碗机门。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:40.82,0:31:42.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it's kind of the same stuff.\N就像是一样的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.46,0:31:46.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh our hypothesis now is that we will see enormous amount of positive transfer from the\N我们现在假设，我们将看到大量积极的迁移效应。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.30,0:31:51.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,data collection efforts we're doing now into pre-training across like basically any environment in the world.\N我们现在正在进行的数据收集工作，将用于预训练，覆盖全球几乎任何环境。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.91,0:32:00.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean that'll be like it'll be somewhat um you know we we'll we'll approach that somewhat like um it'll take I would say over time a large\N嗯，我的意思是，那会有点像，我们会以某种方式去应对，我认为这需要很长时间，而且规模会很大。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.41,0:32:03.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,amount of data to to find every out of distribution like basically be able to\N用于发现所有分布外数据的大量数据，基本上能够实现
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.03,0:32:06.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,do everything possible in the world but we think there's a path to do this.\N尽一切可能，但我们认为有办法实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.79,0:32:12.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what is the price point differentiation for the inhome robot versus commercial?\N家用机器人与商用机器人的价格定位差异是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.32,0:32:16.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the inhome like we we have we're not selling right now to the home.\N呃，家用方面，我们目前并没有向家庭用户销售。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.14,0:32:20.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want we want to sell here uh like in the near term and we want to sell\N我们想在这里短期销售，也想卖出去。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.25,0:32:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robot like for like hundreds of dollars a month and as a like somewhere like a car lease.\N这台机器人每月的租赁费用大约几百美元，就像租一辆车一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.60,0:32:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um maybe like four, five, six hundred bucks a month.\N嗯，大概每月四五百到六百美元吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.24,0:32:29.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,How are you thinking of deploying them in homes?\N您打算如何将它们部署到家庭中？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.89,0:32:33.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like do you have to see if people have enough room like in New York City?\N比如说，你得看看在纽约市，人们有没有足够的空间？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.66,0:32:35.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I can't imagine these little apartments.\N是啊，我无法想象这些小公寓。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.68,0:32:37.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh they just takes a dock.\N嗯，它只需要一个充电座。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.23,0:32:38.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like 2 feet by 2 feet.\N就像两英尺乘两英尺那么大。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.91,0:32:40.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you can plug it in a wall outlet.\N嗯，你可以插到墙上的插座里。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.03,0:32:42.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It'll go to its dock and charge.\N它会自己回到充电座上充电。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.52,0:32:44.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then throughout the day, it'll just go off and do work.\N然后一整天，它就会自己出去干活。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.79,0:32:45.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,What?\N什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.04,0:32:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whatever you want to go want it to do.\N你想让它做什么都可以。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.72,0:32:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like for me, I wanted to do like the laundry probably almost every day, dishes every day, and tidy the house multiple times a day.\N比如我，我几乎每天想洗衣服，每天洗碗，一天多次整理屋子。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.68,0:32:55.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do they have a distinctive diet?\N它们有特别的饮食吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.10,0:32:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do they eat?\N它们吃些什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.92,0:32:57.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They eat nothing.\N他们什么也不吃。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.52,0:32:58.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're keto.\N他们是生酮饮食。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.08,0:32:59.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,They just work 247.\N他们全天候工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.28,0:33:00.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're just constantly intermittent fasting.\N他们一直在断断续续地禁食。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.89,0:33:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're in this like they're in this like uh they're in this like purgatory state of just working 24/7 for us their lives.\N他们处于一种状态，就像他们被困在炼狱里，只为我们的利益而全天候工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.80,0:33:07.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.60,0:33:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.24,0:33:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Fun.\N有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.96,0:33:09.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.37,0:33:09.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.77,0:33:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to next go show you how we make them over at Baku.\N我接下来想带你们去巴库，看看我们是怎么制造它们的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.60,0:33:13.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.86,0:33:14.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great.\N很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.16,0:33:15.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go.\N开始吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.28,0:33:18.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's uh you know like kind of like HQ but Baku.\N就像 HQ 那样，但这里是巴库。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.72,0:33:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't HQ for bots.\N我不给机器人 HQ。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.40,0:33:21.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's bot.\N哦，是机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.60,0:33:21.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.95,0:33:22.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bot.\N机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.24,0:33:23.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought you were saying Baku.\N我还以为你说的是巴库。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.92,0:33:26.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. Isn't BQ.\N不是。是 BotQ。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.08,0:33:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,BotQ.\NBotQ。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.72,0:33:28.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. Anyways, this is BotQ.\N不是。不管怎样，这是 BotQ。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.92,0:33:30.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is BotQ.\N这就是 BotQ。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.56,0:33:30.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.78,0:33:37.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,one thing that's really cool is on the way is uh we we we uh we work at BMW and last\N一件特别酷的事是，我们正在为宝马工作，接下来会有更多进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.42,0:33:43.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,year we h we deployed uh for six months robots on the uh basically body shop factory line to build cars.\N我们部署了机器人，在车身车间的生产线上运行了六个月，用于制造汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.68,0:33:44.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.24,0:33:47.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and this was the first you built this entire car.\N嗯，这还是你第一次打造整辆汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.20,0:33:49.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, not the entire thing, but we helped build this car.\N不，不是整个车，但我们参与打造了这辆车。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.95,0:33:50.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.38,0:33:56.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is an X3 uh that we helped basically uh like we basically helped the robot helped assemble it and this was\N呃，这是个 X3，我们基本上帮了忙，就是我们帮机器人完成了组装，这个就是
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.29,0:34:02.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the first car in the world built by a humanoid robot that we that we're aware of and straight off the assembly line.\N我们所知的世界上第一辆由人形机器人制造并直接从装配线上下线的汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.08,0:34:04.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Straight off as I actually I bought the first four.\N说实话，我确实买了前四款。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.24,0:34:04.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.64,0:34:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have three here on campus and I have one at my house.\N校园里有三台，我家里有一台。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.20,0:34:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh yeah, it's like a collector's item now.\N而且呃，现在它就像一件收藏品了。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.80,0:34:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's exciting.\N这真令人兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.44,0:34:13.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's pretty pretty interesting.\N是的，相当有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.28,0:34:15.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.42,0:34:19.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so we have uh this is kind of our our campus here.\N呃，我们这里有呃，这是我们这边的园区。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.55,0:34:21.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have four buildings.\N我们有四栋楼。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:21.51,0:34:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're going to go through our manufacturing site which is BotQ.\N呃，我们将参观我们的制造基地，也就是 BotQ。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.52,0:34:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we also have a site uh up here that I'll show you uh called the grid.\N然后我们还在这里有一个站点，我稍后会向你们展示，叫作“电网”。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.72,0:34:31.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.04,0:34:36.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the goal of that facility is to run robots like just like we would at our client sites.\N那个设施的目标是像在客户现场一样运行机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.22,0:34:40.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could be in the home and also in the commercial side and 247 operations.\N可以在家庭场景中，也可以在商业场景中，实现全天候 24/7 运营。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.72,0:34:41.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why is it called the grid?\N为什么叫它“电网”？
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.84,0:34:45.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's a kind of a nod to like a sci-fi movie.\N呃，这有点像是向科幻电影致敬。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.38,0:34:47.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and um I don't know.\N呃，呃，我不知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.34,0:34:50.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you have a lot of inspiration from sci-fi movies?\N你从科幻电影里获得很多灵感吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.24,0:34:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you a sci-fi geek?\N你是科幻迷吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.84,0:34:52.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Total sci-fi geek.\N完全的科幻迷。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:52.88,0:34:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I've seen every sci-fi movie.\N我看完了每一部科幻电影。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.72,0:34:55.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's your favorite?\N你最喜欢的电影是哪一部？
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.84,0:34:58.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, probably Contact.\N呃，可能是《接触》。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.22,0:35:00.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jodyie Foster, the alien thing.\N琼·普洛特福斯特，那个外星人故事。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.88,0:35:01.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:01.12,0:35:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of embarrassing to say, but why?\N说这个有点尴尬，但为什么呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.60,0:35:04.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, I don't know.\N呃，我不知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.69,0:35:06.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I just I The contact's amazing.\N我 just 我，这联系太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.48,0:35:07.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you like it, don't be embarrassed.\N如果你喜欢，别不好意思。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.84,0:35:08.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.19,0:35:10.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, but like I'll just I'll watch I'm a sci-fi junkie.\N呃，不过我就是个科幻迷。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.98,0:35:12.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll watch any kind of sci-fi.\N我什么类型的科幻都看。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.71,0:35:13.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, yeah.\N呃，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.57,0:35:16.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh, so that's the grid up here.\N所以，呃，这就是上面的电网。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.45,0:35:21.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and we we'll run robots in that facility 247.\N呃，我们会在那个设施里全天候运行机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.20,0:35:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the goal of that is, uh, last line of defense before we send out any code to our customers.\N目的是在向客户发送任何代码之前，作为最后一道防线。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.52,0:35:31.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you don't want robots, uh, you know, you don't want you don't want like robots having any problems.\N所以，你不想让机器人，呃，你知道，不想让机器人出问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.86,0:35:36.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want to run them close enough to like heavy operations that we would see out in the real world.\N我们希望让它们运行得足够接近真实世界中的重负载操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:36.29,0:35:41.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we have a whole facility dedicated to basically running robots as hard as possible, 247.\N所以，我们有一个专门的设施，基本上全天候地让机器人以极限强度运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.33,0:35:45.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we run on holidays, weekends, 2 to three in the morning.\N我们在节假日、周末，以及每天凌晨两到三点仍在运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.20,0:35:46.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they just run all day every day.\N他们每天全天候不间断运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:46.40,0:35:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have any escaped?\N有逃脱的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.68,0:35:53.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, we've we've had one almost escaped and we really No, nothing's nothing's escaped.\N没有，我们曾有一台几乎逃脱，但最终没有，没有任何设备真正逃脱过。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.36,0:35:55.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do they Do you geo fence them within properties?\N你们会通过地理围栏把它们限制在特定区域内吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.96,0:35:57.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like do you do that when you set them up?\N比如说，你们在设置时会这样做吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.84,0:35:58.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we track them.\N我们会追踪它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.50,0:36:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, this is like for us right now it's like a these are like high IP, right?\N显然，现在对我们来说，这些设备价值很高，属于高价值资产，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.32,0:36:03.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh like very complicated hardware.\N嗯，就像非常复杂的硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.88,0:36:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't want to get stolen or out in the wrong hands.\N我们不希望它们被盗或落入错误的人手中。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.24,0:36:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh so we track it.\N所以，我们就在追踪它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.76,0:36:08.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Has that happened before?\N这种情况之前发生过吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.83,0:36:10.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are people stealing your IP?\N有人窃取你的知识产权吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:10.40,0:36:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we do a lot of work on security internally here.\N嗯，我们在这里内部做了大量安全相关的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.78,0:36:17.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so we haven't had any known IP thefts at the company.\N嗯，公司至今没有发生过已知的知识产权被盗事件。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:17.84,0:36:18.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.24,0:36:18.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.82,0:36:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.88,0:36:21.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to Baku.\N欢迎来到巴库。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.52,0:36:22.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.40,0:36:23.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, oh my god.\N现在，天啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.52,0:36:25.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, welcome to Baku.\N现在，欢迎来到巴库。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.68,0:36:31.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so this is where we uh this is where we manufacture uh Figure 03 robots.\N嗯，这里就是我们制造 Figure 03 机器人的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.44,0:36:31.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.00,0:36:40.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so we uh we do everything from build heads, batteries, legs, arms, fingers, thumbs, hands.\N嗯，我们做所有东西，从头部、电池、腿、手臂、手指、大拇指到手。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.20,0:36:45.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, and we basically do all testing here before we box the robots out or they walk next door.\N嗯，我们在把机器人打包送出或它们走到隔壁之前，基本上都在这里完成所有测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.28,0:36:46.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,What does a box look like?\N一个箱子长什么样？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.40,0:36:46.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,A box?\N一个箱子？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.70,0:36:47.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.96,0:36:47.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, we'll show you.\N嗯，我们马上给你看。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.82,0:36:49.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have one over there in in a minute.\N我们一会儿就在那边展示一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.44,0:36:49.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really?\N真的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.84,0:36:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and right now we basically if we need them at headquarters or the grid, they basically just walk over.\N嗯，现在如果总部或电网需要它们，它们基本上直接走过去就行。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.76,0:36:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where do you store them?\N你们把它们存放在哪里？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.96,0:36:58.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, at the at the office or client sites.\N嗯，在办公室或客户现场。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.16,0:36:58.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.48,0:36:58.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.80,0:36:59.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, on on the docks.\N嗯，在码头上。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.90,0:37:03.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,They basically dock at nighttime or when they're not not needed.\N他们基本上在夜间或不需要时停靠。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.33,0:37:03.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, okay.\N嗯，好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.85,0:37:06.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to show you some of the manufacturing lines.\N我们将向您展示一些生产线。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.36,0:37:16.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we start first uh with basically head and uh and battery uh and we do some electronics uh like basically quality and EOL checking.\N我们首先从头和电池开始，做一些电子元件的检测，比如质量检查和下线测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.24,0:37:17.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,EOL is end of line.\NEOL 是下线测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.22,0:37:21.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we make sure we want every single subsystem to go through a bit pretty like pretty crazy test.\N我们确保每个子系统都要经过相当严苛的测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.62,0:37:23.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here's our here's our headline.\N这就是我们的亮点。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.44,0:37:24.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,A rack of heads.\N一排头。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.24,0:37:25.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh rack of heads.\N一排头。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.87,0:37:28.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,So um here here's a head.\N嗯，这里是一个头。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.61,0:37:35.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our heads have um basically uh Bluetooth like Wi-Fi 5G.\N我们的头部基本上具备类似蓝牙、Wi-Fi 和 5G 的功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.38,0:37:38.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have camera systems on on board.\N它们配备了机载摄像头系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:38.05,0:37:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have lights.\N我们有灯光。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.32,0:37:41.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have thermal systems.\N我们有热成像系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:41.16,0:37:42.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have an IMU.\N我们有一个惯性测量单元。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.05,0:37:46.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So basically the head is like basically a lot of sensors in here.\N所以基本上，这个头部内部集成了大量传感器。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.24,0:37:56.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the heads go through a pretty uh like a rigorous test uh here um uh that we've designed uh internally for end of line testing.\N头部在这里会经过一套我们内部设计的严格测试流程，用于产线末端检测。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.52,0:38:03.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So heads here go through a well first is we basically are are flashing software here under the head for the first time.\N所以这里的头部首先会进行首次软件烧录。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.17,0:38:07.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh all the firmware it's going through a calibration process for the cameras.\N所有固件都会经过摄像头的校准流程。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.17,0:38:11.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and then we're basically making sure their head is in a nominal state to basically put onto a robot.\N然后我们基本上要确保头部处于正常状态，以便安装到机器人上。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.02,0:38:13.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So does it getting are we getting signals out of it?\N它能否正常输出信号？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.00,0:38:17.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh does it have any does it have any issues at all or any errors?\N它是否存在任何问题或错误？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.07,0:38:18.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it does we'll try to triage it.\N如果是这样，我们会尝试进行优先级划分。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.61,0:38:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it doesn't we'll end up putting on a robot.\N如果不是，我们就得上机器人了。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.28,0:38:23.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is like when it's first born.\N这就像它刚出生时一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.68,0:38:23.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.98,0:38:27.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like uh it's kind of just like just raw hardware and it goes in here and\N就像是，它只是一堆原始硬件，然后被放进来，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.43,0:38:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,it comes out with software and comes out with all the checks that we can use it with.\N出来时就带有软件，以及我们能使用的全部检测功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.20,0:38:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.76,0:38:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.76,0:38:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:37.28,0:38:40.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,How often do you walk through every part of the campus?\N你每天都会走遍校园的每个角落吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.62,0:38:41.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like uh every day.\N嗯，每天。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.68,0:38:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every day.\N每天。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.32,0:38:43.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every day.\N每天。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.15,0:38:45.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so here is uh here's our battery line.\N嗯，这里就是我们的电池生产线。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.03,0:38:53.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have battery cells that come in uh and then we basically do uh cell testing and uh like basically voltage balancing.\N我们有电池单体进来，然后我们基本上会进行电池测试，比如电压均衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.97,0:39:01.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So here we're basically checking every single cell against the data sheet and we're also checking voltage and we're balancing out the packs.\N这里我们基本上是把每个电池单体都和数据表对比，同时检查电压，并对电池组进行均衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:01.31,0:39:04.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if there's any um like kind of voltage differential.\N如果有任何电压差异的话。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.68,0:39:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're basically uh making sure that all the packs basically have somewhat of a somewhat balanced voltage.\N我们基本上是在确保所有电池组的电压都大致均衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.04,0:39:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where do you get this machine from?\N这台机器你是从哪里弄来的？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.04,0:39:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We designed this machine.\N我们自己设计了这台机器。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.08,0:39:12.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah.\N哦，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.98,0:39:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,This was custom designed uh for uh for figure here for battery and then uh we go through a process for uh for potting um uh like wire bonding and\N这是为 Figure 定制设计的电池生产线，然后我们进入灌封工序，比如引线键合和
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.08,0:39:28.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's some polyurethane we put inside the battery pack for thermal runaway and then at\N在电池组内部注入一些聚氨酯，用于防止热失控，然后在
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.10,0:39:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,the end pops out uh basically a pretty heavy uh 2.25 kilowatt hour battery pack.\N最后，出来的是一个相当重的、2.25千瓦时的电池组。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.88,0:39:35.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.09,0:39:35.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't even want to try.\N我甚至都不想试。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.99,0:39:37.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really quite heavy.\N这玩意儿真的很重。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.44,0:39:38.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah.\N哦，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.80,0:39:41.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I I don't think it's Wait, let me try.\N不，我不觉得它……等等，让我试试。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.52,0:39:43.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, no. That is actually really heavy.\N哦，天哪。这实际上真的很重。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.48,0:39:48.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this uh so this battery uh will basically go right into the torso.\N所以，这个……这个电池基本上会直接放进躯干里。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.40,0:39:50.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's one of the heaviest components we have.\N这是我们所有组件中最重的一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.80,0:39:51.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.44,0:39:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you I mean I know all this is stabilized, but like is it better that it's one piece in the torso versus distributed across the body?\N你是怎么想的？我是说我知道所有这些都已固定好了，\N但把电池集中放在躯干里，比分散在全身各处，真的更好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:59.44,0:40:01.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's way better one piece.\N嗯，集中放在一处要好得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.22,0:40:04.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The battery pack has um just even for safety,\N电池组……光是出于安全考虑，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.48,0:40:08.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have like a lot of thermal runaway um properties inside the pack that\N电池包内部存在大量热失控特性
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.44,0:40:12.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,we've designed here internally to make sure um in the worst case you basically want\N我们在这里内部设计，以确保在最坏情况下，你基本上想要的
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.68,0:40:19.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh to say like okay if the battery if a cell or battery cell is going to thermal runaway you never want that to ever propagate outside the pack.\N嗯，比如说，如果电池单体或电池单元要发生热失控，你肯定不希望这种状况蔓延到电池包外部。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.20,0:40:21.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you wanted to contain it to the battery system itself.\N所以你是想把它限制在电池系统本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:21.37,0:40:25.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have a basically a structural uh system and also basically a thermway\N所以我们基本上有一个结构化系统，同时也基本上有一个热通道。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.44,0:40:29.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,venting process we've designed internally to basically allow for the battery to be extremely safe.\N我们内部设计的排气工艺，基本上能让电池极为安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.55,0:40:32.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the the requirement is like you want no flame to never exit the pack.\N就像要求一样，你希望火焰永远不要离开火堆。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.95,0:40:36.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't want a robot like on fire or something like that out in the world.\N你不想让一个着火的机器人之类的东西出现在世界上。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:36.34,0:40:38.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we've designed the right safety system.\N所以我们设计了合适的安全系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.88,0:40:41.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we've never had a robot ever have catch fire.\N我们从未有过机器人着火的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.52,0:40:47.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. No. And then our all of our figure 3s are designed in a way that basically will prevent the robot from ever catching fire.\N不，不会。我们的所有 Figure 3 机器人都经过了特殊设计，基本上可以防止机器人起火。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.60,0:40:47.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.01,0:40:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so that that actually was a cra pretty crazy hard engineering feat that we've designed here internally.\N所以实际上，这是我们内部设计的一个相当疯狂且极具挑战性的工程壮举。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.44,0:40:56.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um also the the the pack is structural take loads.\N另外，这个电池包本身也承担结构载荷。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.98,0:41:02.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So in case we fall even on like sharp objects or corners and things like this like we can never propagate inside the pack uh\N所以即使我们撞到尖锐物体或角落之类的东西，也不会导致内部发生传播。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.86,0:41:10.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,the cells itself meaning you don't want anything to uh kind of like uh kind of like send the battery cells itself into thermal away conditions.\N电池本身意味着你不想让任何东西导致电池进入热失控状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.56,0:41:15.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have you had any supply chain risks whether it's with China or other countries?\N你有没有遇到过供应链风险，无论是来自中国还是其他国家？
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.21,0:41:16.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is that why you do everything here?\N所以你才把所有事情都放在这里做吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:41:16.62,0:41:20.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do most of the manufacturing here because the product is so new and it needs to\N我们大部分制造都在这里进行，因为产品非常新，需要严格控制。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.77,0:41:25.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,be really controlled and we also need uh we also think about IP as really important here.\N我们也认为知识产权在这里至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.25,0:41:27.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we don't want any of the technologies to be stolen.\N我们不希望任何技术被窃取。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.44,0:41:27.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.68,0:41:32.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I think this is just hard too like um we be able to put this thing together through a basically\N我觉得这也很困难，比如我们基本上通过一条全新的供应链，从零开始设计、引入并让它正常运行，这并不简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.20,0:41:35.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,a brand new supply chain that we had to design and get it in and make it work is like it's non-trivial.\N这不是一件小事。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:36.02,0:41:38.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like you see how much testing we do at headquarters for all this work.\N就像你看到的，我们在总部为所有这些工作做了大量测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.80,0:41:40.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh testing we do at the grid.\N我们在电网上的测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.56,0:41:42.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll do a ton of testing we'll show you here today.\N今天我们会做大量测试，向你们展示。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.52,0:41:48.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's uh it's enormous and the product is um we're kind of like early in the humanoid kind of like chapter book.\N这非常庞大，而产品本身，我们还处于人形机器人这个章节的早期阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.00,0:41:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so like uh car has been around for over a century.\N就像汽车已经存在了一个多世纪。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.84,0:41:54.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,We kind of the company has been around for four years.\N我们公司才成立四年。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.19,0:41:54.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. Yeah.\N不，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.84,0:41:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not even four years yet.\N还不到四年。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.32,0:41:57.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.12,0:42:01.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then humanoids are like really uh like really early in that whole process.\N而人形机器人在整个进程中，还处于非常早期的阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.44,0:42:04.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,How did you We'll talk about this more in the long form,\N你是怎么做到的？我们稍后会在长篇内容中深入讨论，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.73,0:42:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like in terms of getting this up to scale so fast like you have now created a humanoid robot.\N但就目前而言，如何这么快就实现规模化，你已经创造出一个人形机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.64,0:42:17.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is one of the most complex robot like I don't know engineering problems ever.\N这是我所知的最复杂的机器人，没有之一，工程难题之多令人难以想象。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.19,0:42:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like how did you get up to speed so fast?\N那你是怎么这么快就上手的？
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.40,0:42:25.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um my company before this designed like flying robots at Archer and it's got the same properties.\N嗯，我之前所在的公司曾设计过飞行机器人，就是阿彻公司的，它们具备类似的特性。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:25.31,0:42:30.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a battery pack but instead of like uh 2 kilowatt hours, it's 160 kilowatt hours and it's distributed.\N我们有一个电池组，但不是普通的2千瓦时，而是160千瓦时，并且是分布式布局。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:30.55,0:42:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have electric motors, we have control software, we have embedded systems and sensors.\N我们有电动机，有控制软件，有嵌入式系统和传感器。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.84,0:42:35.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's a robot.\N这就是一台机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.80,0:42:41.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And like Archer's aircrafts, uh like my aircrafts there at like say midnight are like highly overactuated.\N就像阿彻的飞机一样，我设计的飞机在午夜时分也处于高度过驱动状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.60,0:42:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,All the propellers uh at variable pitch.\N所有螺旋桨都具备可变桨距功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.48,0:42:47.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the front leading edge actuators tilt 90 degrees.\N前缘执行器可以旋转90度。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:47.78,0:42:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have uh the flaps uh on the wings and tail all move.\N机翼和尾翼上的襟翼全部都可以移动。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.12,0:42:52.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have like basically 24 degrees of freedom.\N你基本上有24个自由度。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.04,0:42:55.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have about over a little over 40 here on the robot.\N这台机器人则有超过40个自由度。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:55.81,0:43:01.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So um so in some way it's like um like similar enough systems here.\N所以呃，某种程度上，这里的系统有点类似。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:01.33,0:43:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then you know when I started figure we we were like uh we have a very crisp and clear vision for the how to think about the product and\N呃，然后你知道，当我开始做 Figure 时，\N我们当时就明确地有了一个非常清晰的愿景，关于如何思考产品和工程路线图。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.64,0:43:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,engineering roadmap and we just like went like went really hard building a team to\N我们就全力以赴，组建团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.84,0:43:16.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,40 and uh putting the right resources in place for us to design stuff really fast.\N40人，然后为我们配置了合适的资源，以实现快速设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:16.33,0:43:20.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had the we we'll show you here next visit but we have our Figure 01 robot.\N我们接下来会向你们展示，但我们已经有了 Figure 01 机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.26,0:43:21.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it's kind of gnarly.\N它有点粗糙。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.50,0:43:22.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got wires everywhere.\N到处都是电线。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.53,0:43:23.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's our first generation.\N这是我们第一代产品。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.86,0:43:28.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had that walking before we were uh a year old and we think it's probably one of the fastest times in human history.\N我们在不到一岁时就实现了行走，我们认为这可能是人类历史上最快的速度之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:28.76,0:43:33.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it was just like a you know we were like laser focused pedal to the metal trying to get this thing to work.\N所以我们就是全神贯注，全力以赴，只为了把这东西搞出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.28,0:43:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.76,0:43:34.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.01,0:43:34.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.26,0:43:35.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let me show you some more stuff.\N让我给你们看看更多内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:35.83,0:43:44.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have uh we have a a bunch of different lines here that helps build pelvises install battery compute uh arms legs.\N我们这里有几条不同的生产线，用于组装骨盆、安装电池、计算单元以及手臂和腿部。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:44.18,0:43:47.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh here we're installing the lower leg on top.\N这里我们正在安装下肢。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:47.36,0:43:50.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is there a reason there are humans installing the leg?\N为什么现在是由人工来安装腿部？
Dialogue: 0,0:43:50.12,0:43:53.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, at some point we will have robots doing all of this work.\N之后我们将会用机器人完成所有这些工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.92,0:43:55.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Don't let them hear that.\N别让他们听到这话。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:55.44,0:43:55.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:55.78,0:43:59.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, and we're putting more and more automation in the lines now.\N现在我们正在逐步增加生产线的自动化程度。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.49,0:44:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're we will be shipping robots human our humanoid robots into the production lines here uh this year.\N今年我们将把我们的类人机器人运送到这里，投入生产线上。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:04.72,0:44:08.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um, and yeah, now now we're doing like the lower leg assembly for this robot.\N现在我们正在为这款机器人进行下肢组装。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.62,0:44:11.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at some point today, it will go through some testing.\N今天稍后，它将进入测试环节。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.06,0:44:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll show you in a minute.\N一会儿就让你们看到。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.88,0:44:15.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we'll basically walk over to headquarters and start basically uh helping us either\N然后我们基本上会走到总部，开始帮助我们进行AI开发，或者为客户做用例测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.02,0:44:22.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,do uh like AI development or doing uh use case testing for our customers.\N基本上就是做AI开发，或者为我们的客户做用例测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:22.80,0:44:23.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pretty cool, huh?\N很酷，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.60,0:44:24.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's pretty cool.\N确实很酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.92,0:44:25.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.36,0:44:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.84,0:44:29.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So crazy seeing them get assembled.\N看到它们被组装起来真是太疯狂了。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:29.76,0:44:32.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you worried they're going to become sentient?\N你担心它们会变得有意识吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:44:32.72,0:44:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I I think we'll I think we'll be okay.\N嗯，我觉得我们不会有事的。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:39.92,0:44:45.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,um these things will get really smart like they're they're able to like do what humans can physically and I\N这些东西会变得非常聪明，它们能像人类一样完成物理动作，而且我
Dialogue: 0,0:44:45.67,0:44:51.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,think the neural network uh technologies we're designing are we're trying to give like human common sense to all the robots.\N认为我们正在设计的神经网络技术，正努力为所有机器人赋予人类的常识。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.68,0:44:57.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so in some way uh I think we'll get to add or even beyond human level intelligence in these systems.\N所以某种程度上，我认为我们最终会达到甚至超越人类水平的智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.80,0:45:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It actually might be the case that we we get to artificial general intelligence first in these embodiment.\N事实上，我们可能首先在这些具身系统中实现通用人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.04,0:45:03.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really?\N真的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.68,0:45:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.16,0:45:04.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why?\N为什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.38,0:45:08.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we're able to like this interaction data of like touching the world um and\N因为我们能够获取与世界互动的数据，比如触摸世界，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.09,0:45:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,seeing what happens through trial and error is like um it basically uh mo most of\N通过试错来观察结果，这基本上就是
Dialogue: 0,0:45:13.78,0:45:18.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,human intelligence uh is built this way and I think this is like the last\N人类智能构建的方式，我认为这是实现真正通用人工智能的最后
Dialogue: 0,0:45:18.20,0:45:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,missing piece to get to true AGI is this like real world interaction with our environments.\N一块拼图，即与环境进行真实的现实世界互动。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.96,0:45:25.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, come with me over here.\N好的，跟我来这边。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.01,0:45:27.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm g show you some of the testing work.\N我来给你看看一些测试工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.83,0:45:34.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the robots are basically built uh starting with the pelvis uh torso, head, arms, uh legs and hands.\N所以这些机器人基本上是从骨盆、躯干、头部、手臂、腿部和手开始构建的。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.32,0:45:37.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we basically want to we want to go through like a basically a very\N然后我们基本上想像这样走一遍，基本上非常简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:37.66,0:45:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh strenuous testing process to make sure everything is like working nominally before we send it out.\N严格的测试流程，确保所有功能在发货前都能正常运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.24,0:45:47.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we don't want any like loose cables or bad parts or bad communication.\N所以我们不希望有任何松动的电缆、劣质零件或通信故障。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.47,0:45:51.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we send the robot through what we call a final EOL test or end of line test.\N所以我们把机器人送入我们所谓的最终下线测试，或称生产线末端测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:51.61,0:45:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where the robots go through all the final checks and they basically go through also a burn-in on on these lines.\N这就是机器人进行所有最终检测的地方，它们也在这条线上进行最后的上电老化测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.76,0:45:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you mean by burnin?\N你所说的“burnin”是什么意思？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.88,0:46:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,They'll they'll run for several hours.\N它们会运行好几个小时。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.48,0:46:00.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.80,0:46:04.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we'll basically make sure there's nothing that basically uh no no issues pop\N我们基本上会确保不会出现任何问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.27,0:46:07.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,up over those few hours before we before we send the send the robots out.\N在我们把机器人派出去之前那几个小时里。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.92,0:46:13.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh so here we have um these bays that are running a combination\N嗯，这里我们看到这些机柜正在运行一组组合的系统
Dialogue: 0,0:46:13.49,0:46:17.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,of burn-in testing and uh and end ofline checks that we've designed here internally.\N我们在此内部设计的上电老化测试和下线检查。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.96,0:46:23.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we basically go through a process where the robot's basically self like trying to understand itself like do is anything seem wrong.\N所以我们基本上会经历一个过程，机器人会像自我探索一样，试图理解自己，比如有没有哪里看起来不对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.04,0:46:26.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it is we will uh we'll flag it.\N如果是的话，我们会标记出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:26.15,0:46:29.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it's not basically we go through a process where we basically do like basically\N如果不行的话，我们就进入一个基本上就是基本上这样的过程。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.62,0:46:33.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,a bunch of checks and burn in make sure the robot's in good good condition.\N一系列检测和老化测试确保机器人处于良好状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.68,0:46:40.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um if they pass here we basically uh we'll we'll walk over to headquarters and if they fail here we need to go fix it and understand why.\N如果它们通过这里，我们基本上就直接去总部了；如果它们在这里失败了，我们就得去修复并弄清楚原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.56,0:46:43.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why do these ones have vests on them?\N为什么这些家伙要穿背心？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.20,0:46:45.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, when the robots are getting brought up,\N嗯，当机器人开始启动时，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.45,0:46:54.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,we basically uh we I think we hold it through a gantry system on the back and they have their vests on for that system.\N我们基本上是通过背部的龙门架系统来固定，他们也穿上了该系统的背心。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.56,0:46:57.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's basically like the robots are like just been born and they're waking up.\N感觉就像机器人刚出生，正在苏醒过来。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:57.52,0:47:00.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're saying, you know, they look at they look at their hands,\N他们说，你知道吗，他们会看着自己的手，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.39,0:47:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,they start calibrating itself visually and um try trying to make sure everything's in a healthy state of this campus.\N它们开始进行视觉校准，并尝试确保校园内一切处于健康状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:07.76,0:47:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,What is your favorite part?\N你最喜欢哪一部分？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.56,0:47:14.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Baku is one of my favorite parts here.\N我觉得巴库是这里我最喜欢的地方之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.71,0:47:16.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like being able to build robots.\N就像是能够制造机器人一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:16.88,0:47:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um in March we had record um you know we we we had record manufacturing.\N三月份我们创下了纪录，你知道的，我们实现了创纪录的制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.12,0:47:27.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we we we made more robots in March than we had ever in our entire lifetime combined.\N我们在三月份制造的机器人数量，超过了我们一生中所有时间的总和。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.55,0:47:30.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's just cool to see us being able to do this and then get them out the door.\N看到我们能完成这些，然后把它们送出去，真的太酷了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:31.04,0:47:35.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so I would say um this is probably one of my favorite places in the in the campus.\N所以我认为，这可能是我在校园里最喜欢的地方之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.90,0:47:40.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think maybe my other favorite place that we'll show um some point here is like\N我想我们稍后会展示的另一个我最喜欢的地方是……
Dialogue: 0,0:47:40.05,0:47:45.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robots doing real useful work 247 um on our either commercial customers or in the home.\N机器人全天候不间断地为我们的商业客户或家庭完成真正有用的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:46.01,0:47:50.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that stuff is just amazing because what we're here to do is we're here to like basically build like uh humanlike\N这些东西真是太棒了，因为我们来这里的目的就是，基本上要在这个世界上构建类似人类的
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.01,0:47:56.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,intelligence in the world and to see robots working 247 being able to do things like humans can is like so special.\N智能，看到机器人全天候运行，能够像人类一样做事，这真是太特别了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.71,0:47:57.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like such a hard thing to do.\N这真的是一件非常困难的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:57.92,0:47:58.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:58.17,0:48:02.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And be able to see us doing it like uh at these levels of reliability is like it's awesome.\N而且能亲眼看到我们做到这种程度的可靠性，真是太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.55,0:48:05.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so I think it's probably a couple of my favorite places on campus.\N嗯，我想大概是校园里我最喜欢的几个地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:05.76,0:48:10.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you didn't have your job, what job would you want here?\N如果你没有这份工作，你最想在这里做什么工作？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.16,0:48:15.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think um I think there's a few things I really like.\N嗯，我觉得有几个地方我特别喜欢。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:15.81,0:48:21.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like the engineering design process of how do you think about clean sheet improving the system to be like more reliable,\N我喜欢那种从零开始的工程设计流程，思考如何通过全新设计来提升系统的可靠性。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.03,0:48:28.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,cheaper, lower in mass and um overall a better functioning robot that can do more of what humans can with less complexity.\N更便宜、质量更轻，整体上功能更优，能以更低的复杂度完成更多人类能做的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.77,0:48:36.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that that job across the hardware like engineering and software engineering design or is like I I spent a lot of time\N我认为，跨硬件的工程和软件工程设计工作，就像我花了大量时间那样
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.26,0:48:43.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,in that uh like leading engineering here and it's just like a uh yeah it's just a really fun and I think very hard problem.\N在这里引领工程创新，感觉就像……嗯，这确实是一个非常有趣且极具挑战性的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:43.07,0:48:47.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh everything you try every choice you make to try to make the robot better for thermals or\N你尝试的每一件事，你做出的每一个选择，都是为了提升机器人在热管理方面的表现。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.46,0:48:52.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,better like lower lower mass or like lower weight makes the something else on the other side worse.\N比如降低质量或重量，会让另一侧的某些方面变差。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.50,0:48:57.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you're trying to make the robot like lighter it means it probably can't like hold as much weight. then can't hold as much weight.\N如果想让机器人更轻，就意味着它可能无法承受那么大的重量，也就承载不了那么重的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.99,0:49:03.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,The customers are like, "Well, if you can't carry 30 pound boxes around, I I can't use you on this assembly line."\N客户会说：“如果你连30磅的箱子都搬不动，那我在这条装配线上就用不了你。”
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.26,0:49:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so there's just like um I think there's a lot of just interesting, very hard problems to solve there.\N嗯，我觉得那里有很多有趣且非常棘手的问题需要解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.32,0:49:14.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think second is like how do we get neural networks to run on robots and generalize at scale on the Helix team\N我认为第二点是，我们如何让神经网络在机器人上运行，并在赫利克斯团队实现大规模泛化。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.72,0:49:21.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that for uh really is like a um at this point a data and generalization issue and that's a really hard fun problem.\N这实际上在现阶段是一个数据和泛化问题，也是一个非常困难但有趣的难题。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:21.67,0:49:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh manufacturing is another one of how do we like how do we manufacture robots at scale?\N制造是另一个问题，我们如何实现机器人的规模化制造？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.20,0:49:28.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we continue to get robots in the manufacturing process to build themselves?\N我们如何让机器人持续参与到制造过程中，实现自我建造？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.26,0:49:32.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how do we get them to off the lines into the real world as fast as possible?\N以及我们如何让它们尽快从生产线上走向真实世界？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.24,0:49:36.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,At some point here, it'll just be like a it'll just be full lights out manufacturing.\N从某个阶段开始，这将变成真正的全自动化无人制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.04,0:49:39.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we'll have like robots only building robots and sending out to the world.\N我们将只有机器人在制造机器人，然后把它们送往世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.80,0:49:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,The robots will be getting into boxes themselves.\N机器人自己会进入箱子。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.55,0:49:45.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Other robots will be boxing them up and we'll be shipping them out to customers.\N其他机器人会把它们打包，然后我们再把它们发给客户。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.68,0:49:46.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:46.16,0:49:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sounds a bit sentient.\N听起来有点像有意识了。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.08,0:49:48.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a bit sentient.\N它有点像有意识。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.01,0:49:49.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.28,0:49:53.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh so that's another area where I'm just like um it's extremely interesting.\N所以在这一点上，我觉得非常有意思。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.52,0:49:57.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think the last piece is uh um we have a whole commercial operations team\N我认为最后一点是，我们有一个完整的商业运营团队，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.52,0:50:00.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's trying to get robots out to the world at scale and make them really useful.\N正在努力将机器人大规模推向世界，并让它们真正有用。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:00.78,0:50:05.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we did this uh with BMW last year and we're doing it with more customers this year for Figure 03.\N去年我们和宝马合作过，今年我们正与更多客户合作，推进 Figure 03。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.00,0:50:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's um it's a really cool problem because it's really hard like robots need to get in the environment needs to get safely.\N这是个非常酷的问题，因为真的很难——机器人必须能安全地进入环境。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.04,0:50:14.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They never like basically can almost never fault and when they do fault they need to understand\N它们几乎不能出故障，一旦出故障，就必须能自我识别并纠正。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.52,0:50:18.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,that and self-correct and then we need to be able to do useful human work at human performance.\N然后我们还需要让它们能以人类的水平完成有用的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.82,0:50:24.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So our our comparison is like what does a human do today in terms of speeds inaccuracies um and then reliability.\N所以我们的参照标准是：人类目前在速度、准确性和可靠性方面能做到什么程度。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:24.83,0:50:26.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like that's a hard bar to hit.\N所以这确实是个很难达到的标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.50,0:50:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh those are all like um kind of like gigantic problems to go solve that I think I if I was you know here I'd want to spend all my time on those.\N所以这些都是一些巨大的难题，如果我是你，我肯定会想把所有时间都花在解决这些问题上。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.04,0:50:35.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cool.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.52,0:50:35.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.86,0:50:36.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:36.37,0:50:36.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:36.71,0:50:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want to see the design studio?\N想去看看设计工作室吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.72,0:50:39.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.96,0:50:39.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go.\N我们走吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.36,0:50:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go.\N我们走吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.28,0:50:44.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you think of this?\N你觉得这个怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.56,0:50:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really fun.\N真的很有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.72,0:50:46.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really fun.\N真的很有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.88,0:50:50.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have the coolest job because I just get to visit people's factories all day.\N我有最酷的工作，因为我整天都能去参观别人的工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.56,0:50:50.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.88,0:50:52.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And everybody's building something different.\N每个人都在做不同的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.67,0:50:55.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was at Applied Intuition earlier uh this week.\N本周早些时候我去了 Applied Intuition。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.48,0:50:57.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was then at Skyio.\N然后我去了 Skyio。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:57.30,0:50:59.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I've been to Archer.\N我去过 Archer。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.76,0:51:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I've been to um Anderoll.\N我去过 Anderoll。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.60,0:51:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have just been looking through every door.\N我们 just 在逐一查看每扇门。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.36,0:51:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's awesome.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.44,0:51:11.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.60,0:51:15.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,5 years ago when I took Archer public, um, I saw this campus.\N五年前我让 Archer 上市时，我看到了这个园区。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.32,0:51:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was all empty and I was like, I got to be here.\N当时这里全是空的，我当时就想，我一定要在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.52,0:51:17.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.84,0:51:19.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the the build the buildings are like really big.\N就像那些建筑，真的非常大。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:19.96,0:51:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh like it's just like they're all open.\N呃，就像它们全都敞开着一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:21.96,0:51:25.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just like it's just like and you multiple buildings on campus and they're all\N就像校园里有多栋建筑，它们全都
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.41,0:51:28.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,close and it's it's hard to find space like that where you can build hardware in,\N关闭后，很难找到这样的空间来搭建硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.32,0:51:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,make loud noises, but also close where everybody lives in the Bay Area.\N制造巨大噪音，同时也靠近旧金山湾区每个人的居住地。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:31.20,0:51:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you worried it's too nice?\N你担心它太好了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.36,0:51:34.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh no, not at all.\N天啊，完全不是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:34.77,0:51:42.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like uh we're like we like it looks like we're uh we're manufacturing in here and running robots, so it's it's uh No, it's fine for us.\N嗯，我们好像在这里制造东西，还开着机器人，所以对我们来说没问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.84,0:51:46.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,and like you it it has like like some industrial grit here, you know what I mean?\N而且就像你一样，这里带点工业风的粗犷感，你懂我的意思吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:51:46.57,0:51:49.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It feels uh like we're like we're kind of like builders and makers.\N感觉我们就像是一群建造者和创造者。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.44,0:51:50.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's uh it's kind of nice.\N所以啊，感觉还挺不错的。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.89,0:51:56.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of like reflects a lot about like kind of who we are uh on the team and it's just like my happy place.\N它很能反映我们团队的特质，对我来说，这就是我的快乐之地。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.99,0:51:57.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.28,0:52:03.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Been been looking at this for five years and we finally we finally got it and uh it's great and I can just walk to manufacturing.\N我们已经研究这个项目五年了，终于，终于搞定了，太棒了，我现在可以直接走到制造车间。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:03.65,0:52:04.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can walk to the grid.\N我可以走到电网。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:04.64,0:52:06.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can walk to building four.\N我可以走到四号厂房。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.14,0:52:09.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can walk here to headquarters and I can just be here with my team and pop\N我可以走到这里来总部，和我的团队待在一起，随时需要就过来解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:09.73,0:52:14.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,in where I need uh to solve like any like whatever the biggest problem of the day is.\N比如说当天最大的难题，我随时都能过来处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.48,0:52:18.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is most of your talent down in South Bay or do they all commute?\N你们大部分人才都在南湾吗？还是都通勤过来？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:18.08,0:52:21.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um most of the talent is here and then we have a shuttle for folks in the city that want to come down.\N大部分人才都在这里，然后我们有班车，方便城里的同事过来。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:21.95,0:52:27.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,So maybe like I don't know five or 10% of the of of you know folks here work in like live in the city and commute\N比如说，大概有五到百分之十的人住城里，通勤过来工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.74,0:52:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,down and then I think maybe most majority of the rest all live kind of pretty local within like 20 or 30 minutes from the office.\N然后我觉得剩下的大多数人都住得挺近，大概在办公室二十到三十分钟车程内。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.36,0:52:33.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.64,0:52:35.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Luckily the weather is nice here today.\N幸好今天天气不错。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:35.51,0:52:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean the weather is just freezing and cold and rainy yesterday.\N我的意思是昨天天气真的很冷，又湿又冷还下雨。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:38.72,0:52:39.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:38.96,0:52:39.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.21,0:52:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,The weather is pretty much the same here every day.\N这里的天气每天几乎都一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.72,0:52:44.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's Oh my god, we're back.\N好的，天啊，我们回来了。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:44.64,0:52:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're back so fast.\N我们回来得这么快。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.64,0:52:50.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,How did you come up with the logo?\N你是怎么想到这个标志的？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:50.69,0:52:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.04,0:52:54.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Logo is uh got a couple uh things that are cool here.\N标志里有几个挺酷的点。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:54.40,0:53:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like one is like uh it kind of like looks like um like basically how the robot steps and tracking its steps and feet.\N一个是它看起来有点像机器人走路时的步态，以及追踪它的脚步和脚的位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.12,0:53:01.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.52,0:53:06.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then two, it's like a little F for figure.\N然后第二个是，它有个小小的“F”，代表 Figure。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.48,0:53:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is the fancy secret room now.\N所以，这就是现在那个华丽的秘密房间了。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.64,0:53:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a secret room that nobody's allowed to come in.\N这是一个不允许任何人进入的保密房间。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.64,0:53:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh.\N哦。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:11.44,0:53:13.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is our design studio.\N嗯，这是我们设计工作室。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:14.03,0:53:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'm going to show you every robot we've ever built.\N那么，我要向你们展示我们迄今为止制造过的每一台机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.12,0:53:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.68,0:53:18.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.51,0:53:27.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so we started in 2022 and uh the goal was like how do we get humanoid robots to our AI and software team as fast as possible.\N嗯，我们从2022年开始，目标是尽可能快地把人形机器人送到我们的AI和软件团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.76,0:53:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we designed Figure 01 here.\N嗯，我们设计了这里的Figure 01。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.72,0:53:33.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is our first generation robot.\N这是我们第一代机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.57,0:53:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh pretty cyberpunk.\N嗯，相当赛博朋克风格。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.76,0:53:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how much did this one cost to make and develop going down the line?\N那么这一台从研发到量产，成本是多少？
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.24,0:53:42.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh wow.\N哦天啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.03,0:53:50.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, this one was like uh built to be expensive and move extremely fast uh in terms of building it.\N嗯，这个东西的设计就是为了让它造价高昂，并且在制造过程中能极其快速地完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:50.99,0:53:53.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this was like hundreds of thousands of dollars.\N所以，这差不多花了数十万美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.60,0:54:00.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, and the robots we have now are are like uh uh you know, well under $100,000 each.\N嗯，我们现在拥有的机器人每个价格都不到10万美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:00.56,0:54:08.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and uh so yeah, this was very expensive, mostly expensive because we CNC manufactured the entire thing.\N嗯，所以这个确实非常昂贵，主要是因为我们用CNC加工了整个结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:08.69,0:54:15.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh like basically the way we made all the metal parts was like extremely high precision like think like Formula 1 race car type type type stuff.\N嗯，基本上我们制造所有金属部件的方式都是极高精度的，就像一级方程式赛车那样的水准。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.93,0:54:19.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we had this walk-in within the first year.\N嗯，我们第一年就建成了这个可步入的车间。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:19.22,0:54:23.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and we did we did a lot of the early AI stuff here that we kind of proved out the company.\N嗯，我们在这里完成了早期的很多AI工作，也借此验证了公司的可行性。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:23.27,0:54:24.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was it was great.\N非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.36,0:54:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then we moved on to Figure 02 which is which is here.\N嗯，然后我们转向了Figure 02，它就在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.52,0:54:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh some improvements we did is we moved the battery uh that was on a backpack into the torso.\N我们做的一些改进是，把原本背在背包里的电池移到了躯干里。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.36,0:54:33.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.76,0:54:37.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then this one had like a basically relatively small computer compared to this.\N然后这个相比而言，计算机的规模要小得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.50,0:54:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We basically tripled the compute.\N我们基本上将计算能力提升了三倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.20,0:54:42.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we basically doubled the battery pack, tripled the compute.\N所以我们基本上将电池组容量翻倍，计算能力提升了三倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:42.31,0:54:46.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we have new camera sensors in the head and pelvis in the back.\N嗯，我们在头部和躯干后部新增了摄像头传感器。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:46.27,0:54:52.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we had our next generation hands and uh we basically wired the whole robot internally.\N嗯，我们采用了下一代的手部，并且基本上将整个机器人的内部线路全部连接好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:52.15,0:54:56.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and we also designed uh designed the structure similar to air.\N嗯，我们还设计了类似飞机结构的框架。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:56.17,0:54:59.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Air aircrafts take loads to the aircraft skin.\N飞机的载荷会传递到机身外壳上。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:59.07,0:55:03.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we designed the basically the structure is an exoskeleton.\N所以我们设计的结构基本上是一个外骨骼。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.32,0:55:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So all the load pass uh for the structures is is exterior of the exterior surface.\N所有结构的受力都通过外部表面传递。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:09.04,0:55:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we made about I think like 50 of these and uh we just recently we're just we're just we just recently retired in about a month or two.\N嗯，我们大概制作了五十个这样的原型，最近我们刚刚在一个月或两个月前将其退役。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:17.12,0:55:19.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and then we've moved now to generation three.\N嗯，现在我们已经转向第三代了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.81,0:55:21.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is our Figure 03 robot.\N嗯，这是我们的 Figure 03 机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.88,0:55:24.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Those are all three the same with different outfits.\N这三个都是一样的，只是换了不同的服装。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:24.80,0:55:28.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um the robot here we like reduced we reduced the weight.\N这个机器人我们做了减重处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.52,0:55:31.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,We made it skinnier but also keep the same power and torques.\N我们让它更纤细了，但同时保持了相同的功率和扭矩。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.38,0:55:32.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got Oic speeds.\N它具备奥运级速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:32.54,0:55:33.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got Ozimpic.\N它具备奥运级性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:33.94,0:55:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, exactly.\N没错，正是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:35.44,0:55:36.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I think it looks better.\N我觉得这样看起来更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.68,0:55:40.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like this will look a little too like uh kind of too roboty.\N这样看起来会太像机器人了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.34,0:55:41.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's much robot.\N太像机器人了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:41.40,0:55:42.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Less robot.\N少一点机器人感。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.15,0:55:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Too much robot.\N机器人感太强了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.28,0:55:43.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.72,0:55:45.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like uh so we slimmed everything down.\N就是啊，我们把所有东西都简化了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:45.68,0:55:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We soft wrapped it.\N我们用软材料包裹了它。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.72,0:55:49.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got a layer of foam like on the shoulders and to the chest.\N它在肩部和胸部都有泡沫层。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:49.94,0:55:50.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's soft.\N所以很柔软。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:50.77,0:55:56.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have our next we have our newest generation hands on this which have camera tactile sensors.\N我们这次用上了最新一代的手部，带有摄像头和触觉传感器。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.33,0:55:59.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh is basically able to grasp items much much easier.\N基本上能更轻松地抓取物品。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.66,0:56:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we reduced the cost by about 90% between these two.\N我们在这两个版本之间把成本降低了大约90%。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.36,0:56:03.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really?\N真的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.92,0:56:04.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.28,0:56:04.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ex.\N例如。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.52,0:56:04.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.88,0:56:06.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,What was the major cost there?\N那里的主要成本是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.40,0:56:11.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we didn't care like we've optimized these first few generations for speed.\N嗯，我们当时并不太在意成本，因为前几代产品我们已经针对速度进行了优化。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.92,0:56:13.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We didn't care as much about cost.\N我们对成本的考量没有那么大。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:13.44,0:56:18.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that was like the biggest misconception of designing it initially with speed.\N所以最初设计时过于追求速度，这是最大的误解。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.56,0:56:18.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.88,0:56:21.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I we were sitting here in 2022.\N就像我们当时坐在2022年。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.10,0:56:28.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're like um our software folks need a humanoid to do testing and do AI work or whatever it is on it.\N我们觉得，我们的软件团队需要一个人形机器人来完成测试，或者在上面做AI相关的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.12,0:56:33.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and there's like there wasn't at the time uh still really isn't a good humanoid robot to go by to help us speed us up.\N当时还没有一个足够好的人形机器人可供参考，来帮助我们加快进度。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:33.98,0:56:35.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we had to go build it.\N所以我们只能自己动手去造。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.10,0:56:37.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's like even if it's expensive like let's get stuff to the team as fast\N所以即使成本高，也要尽快把东西交给团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.89,0:56:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,as possible to start getting like the basically start like working on the development process for commercialization.\N尽快开始推进商业化开发流程。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:42.64,0:56:48.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the same with figure 2 the goal was like um we had a lot of problems with reliability here that we needed to clean up.\N同样地，对于Figure 2，目标是解决这里存在的大量可靠性问题，需要彻底清理。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:48.40,0:56:52.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had like wires poking out and all kinds of issues here with this robot.\N这个机器人存在电线外露等各种问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.08,0:56:55.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it was kind of it was kind of falting every few hours.\N嗯，它每隔几个小时就会出现一些故障。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.19,0:56:55.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.45,0:57:01.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,so we just had a ton of reliability issues we needed to clean up because we're kind of known though because we're moving really really really fast.\N所以我们遇到了大量可靠性问题，需要解决，毕竟我们进展得太快了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.06,0:57:05.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So Figure 02 was just like way too expensive, like too hard to manufacture at scale.\N所以 Figure 02 实在是太贵了，大规模制造也太难了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:05.66,0:57:09.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So Figure 03 was like how do we like reduce the cost by like almost an order of magnitude?\N所以 Figure 03 就是想，我们怎么才能把成本降低将近一个数量级？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.35,0:57:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we make a lot of them?\N我们怎么才能大量生产它们？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.64,0:57:14.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we make it like closer to what we think the ideal outcome is for like every robot in the world?\N我们怎么才能让它更接近我们心目中全球每台机器人都该有的理想状态？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.64,0:57:18.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so these robots uh basically have the ability to take these clothes on and off.\N嗯，这些机器人基本上能自己穿脱衣服。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.70,0:57:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have different like different different types of um accessories we can put on them.\N我们可以给它们安装各种不同的配件。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.16,0:57:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh shoes, gloves, uh like yeah, fabrics.\N比如鞋子、手套，还有各种布料。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.04,0:57:31.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,How often are you thinking about the next version?\N你多久会考虑下一代产品？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.70,0:57:34.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what do you want the next version to be?\N你希望下一代产品是什么样的？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.47,0:57:37.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And like do you start thinking about it while you're building this one or after it?\N就像你在建造这个的时候就开始思考这个问题，还是之后才开始？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.04,0:57:41.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like at what point of the production stage do you start the next iteration?\N在生产阶段的哪个节点，你会开始下一个迭代？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.82,0:57:47.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we are now building a new robot almost every year and uh we'll have uh you know we\N我们现在几乎每年都在打造一台新机器人，而且我们很快就会……你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:47.81,0:57:54.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,we were like we're like late stage now in the design process for Figure 04 and um there are\N我们现在正处于 Figure 04 的设计后期阶段，而且有一些
Dialogue: 0,0:57:54.11,0:57:58.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,some changes that we like we want to put into the iterate this is like a it's like this\N我们想要加入的改动，我们想对它进行迭代，这就像
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.08,0:58:02.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,is like iPhone like iPhones you know what I mean like everyone's getting better yeah exactly uh so every\N就像 iPhone 一样，你知道我的意思吧？每个人都在变得更好，对吧？完全正确，所以每
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.99,0:58:06.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,word we're trying to get better so there there are some things we just didn't get to and have\N一次我们都在努力变得更好，有一些事情我们之前没来得及完成，也没足够时间在 Figure 03 上
Dialogue: 0,0:58:06.75,0:58:10.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,enough time to work on on Figure 03 that we want to derisk we put into four uh And\N去处理，现在我们把这些风险降低的改进都放进 Figure 04 里了。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.94,0:58:14.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,there are also some things we've learned from like operating Figure 03 now that we're like man this is\N同时，我们也从现在运行 Figure 03 的过程中学到了一些东西，\N比如“天啊，如果当初我们这么做，会好得多”。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:14.46,0:58:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,like could be way better if we did this for that that we're putting into Figure 04 as well.\N这些经验我们也都应用到了 Figure 04 上。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.76,0:58:22.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we want to keep reducing costs and making it easier to manufacture at every step.\N然后我们还想持续降低成本，让每一步的制造都更简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.14,0:58:25.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're looking at Figure 04 and we're like uh Figure 03 we're like oh\N所以我们看 Figure 04，就会想：Figure 03，我们当时真是……
Dialogue: 0,0:58:25.32,0:58:28.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,man like some of these things are like kind of hard to manufacture at BCube.\N有些人觉得这些部件在BCube上制造起来有点困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.82,0:58:34.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um or like how are we going to get it out of a box or how are we going to get it like a new user in a home like really easily.\N或者说我们该怎么把它从盒子里拿出来，或者怎么让新用户在家轻松上手。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.04,0:58:38.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like taking all those collective like learnings and we're putting them into the engineering design efforts and\N所以我们将所有这些集体经验教训融入到工程设计中。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:38.87,0:58:43.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,we go through many different like basically gating processes for that for like starting with like an architecture\N我们会经历多个基本的筛选流程，从系统架构设计开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:43.36,0:58:47.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,review of what what the system should look like and high level like you know like level zero\N评估系统应该是什么样子，以及高层次的，比如零级要求。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:47.54,0:58:52.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,requirements all the way through to detail design which we're we're now in for figure uh Figure 04.\N一直推进到详细设计阶段，我们现在正处于Figure 04的这个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:52.26,0:58:59.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's kind of crazy here is um I thought at some point we like we would saturate out like an you know iPhone like doesn't really change much anymore.\N这里有点疯狂的是，我曾以为我们迟早会达到一个瓶颈，就像iPhone那样，已经基本不再有大的变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:59.33,0:59:02.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought like Figure 03 at this point was like this is like a this is like our best human\N我曾认为Figure 03目前就是我们全球最好的人形机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:02.80,0:59:06.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,robot in the world and is every robot's going to be like it's going to be better but not by much.\N所有其他机器人将会变得更好，但提升幅度不会太大。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:06.55,0:59:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's going to happen here is you're going to have Figure 01 kind of a you know\N这里会发生的是，Figure 01到Figure 02会是一次明显的提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.44,0:59:13.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,to Figure 02 like a step up and Figure 02 to Figure 03 at a step up.\NFigure 02到Figure 03也会是一次显著的提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:13.86,0:59:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Figure 04 will be the biggest step up we've ever made by far.\NFigure 04将是迄今为止我们迈出的最大一步。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:17.44,0:59:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll have it out here at one point and you'll be like oh my gosh it's just like radically different.\N我们迟早会把它拿出来，到那时你会惊讶地发现，它简直天差地别。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:22.51,0:59:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um so we obviously can't talk too much.\N而且呃，我们显然不能说得太多。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:24.82,0:59:27.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can't talk about anything basically on on what we're doing there.\N我们基本上没法谈论我们在那里做的任何事。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:27.60,0:59:29.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,But like uh we are just so early.\N但说实话，我们还处于非常早期的阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:29.26,0:59:33.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're like almost in like flip phones and now we're entering like iPhone one moment.\N我们就像刚从翻盖手机时代走出来，现在正进入iPhone 1时刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:33.35,0:59:37.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think maybe Figure 04 will be our first like iPhone one moment for this where it's just like\N我觉得Figure 04可能会成为我们这一代的iPhone 1时刻，它将彻底与众不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:37.38,0:59:44.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,radically different and probably like for me I think it's like almost the perfect humanoid robot I can think of.\N对我来说，它几乎就是我能想到的最完美的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:44.40,0:59:47.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sure there's things on five and six as we iterate through it'll be even better.\N我相信随着我们不断迭代，第五代和第六代会变得更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:47.86,0:59:49.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but we've learned a lot.\N呃，但我们已经学到了很多。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:49.92,0:59:52.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here's a couple examples we have.\N这里有几个例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:52.50,0:59:57.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, here's some parts we have on the table for uh this is our generation of hands.\N呃，这些是我们桌上的一些部件，这是我们这一代的手。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.36,1:00:00.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Starting with our first generation hand to our current generation hand today.\N从第一代手到我们今天所用的当前代手。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.04,1:00:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've gone through like five uh versions of this kind of well they're kind of like same size as my hands.\N我们已经经历了大约五代这种手，它们大小差不多和我的手差不多。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.80,1:00:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that one.\N就是那个。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:07.52,1:00:10.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, one thing we have never shown is our first generation hand.\N有一件事我们从未展示过，就是我们的第一代手。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.40,1:00:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really?\N真的吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.88,1:00:11.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:11.28,1:00:11.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why?\N为什么？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:11.92,1:00:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, was really difficult from an IP perspective and engineering perspective to go build.\N呃，从知识产权和工程角度来说，要把它做出来非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:16.40,1:00:21.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and two is we think um we learned a lot about it and we learned like things like what are good and good and bad.\N呃，第二点是，我们认为我们从中学到了很多，比如哪些地方做得好，哪些地方不好。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:21.91,1:00:27.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,In this case we felt like we had um uh learned a lot about the hand of like why it's probably not the right direction.\N在这种情况下，我们觉得已经充分了解了手的设计，明白它可能并不是正确的方向。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:27.67,1:00:31.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So our first generation hand you can see here is a tendon driven hand.\N所以你们看到的第一代手，是一个肌腱驱动的手。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:31.28,1:00:36.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah we designed all the motors and actuators here ourselves uh even the gearboxes.\N是的，我们自己设计了所有的电机和执行器，甚至连变速箱也是。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:36.63,1:00:39.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh basically the the rationale here is that a human hands like this.\N呃，基本的思路是，人类的手就是这样的。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:39.73,1:00:45.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our most of our motors are on our forearm and they're basically we're like uh little like uh tendons basically driving all the\N我们大部分的电机都安装在前臂上，它们的作用就像肌腱一样，驱动所有手指。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.36,1:00:51.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,fingers and um so our first generation hand is like how do we get a really dextrous hand built which is like really\N我们的第一代手部设计是：如何打造一个非常灵巧的手，这种手对智能和人工智能非常有帮助。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.68,1:00:57.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,good for intelligence and AI and uh and then uh ultimately that can do a lot of things that human can and how\N并且最终能够完成人类能做的许多事情。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.29,1:01:03.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,do we mimic the biological kind of architecture of a human and um so I was like this is going to be great.\N我们如何模仿人类生物结构的架构？我觉得这会是个很棒的方案。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:03.53,1:01:04.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to put motors in here.\N我们打算把电机放在这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:04.62,1:01:05.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to be really powerful.\N它们会非常强劲。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.71,1:01:10.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,are going to drive a really high degree of freedom hand and ended up becoming uh ended\N能驱动一个自由度极高的手，但结果发现这其实是个错误的工程选择。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.16,1:01:15.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,up becoming like the wrong engineering choice and we end up pivoting away from it really early.\N我们不得不很早就放弃这个方案，转向其他方向。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.52,1:01:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh most of the wrist motors are also in here.\N大部分腕部电机也在这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:18.64,1:01:21.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So on Figure 01, I don't know if you noticed, but the wrists look crazy.\N在 Figure 01 上，你可能没注意到，但腕部看起来很奇怪。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:21.79,1:01:26.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for this is that we pivoted away really early away from this tendon driven hand, right?\N原因是我们在很早阶段就放弃了这种肌腱驱动的手部设计，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:26.64,1:01:29.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had to figure out a way to get like new motors in for the wrist.\N我们必须找到一种方法，为腕部安装新的电机。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:29.84,1:01:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh, instead of waiting like four months to redesign those from scratch, um, I took the the motors from the feet.\N所以，与其等上四个月重新从头设计，我干脆把脚上的电机拆下来用了。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:36.48,1:01:43.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we have three foot motors here in the forearm, and it's just like this Frankenstein forearm, and it like it bends like in mid like,\N所以，前臂这里有三个脚部电机，这就像是个弗兰肯斯坦式的手臂，它就像这样在中间弯曲，
Dialogue: 0,1:01:43.54,1:01:49.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, the the instead of bending here at the wrist, it bends like halfway through the forearm, which is just like really weird.\N本来应该在手腕处弯曲，结果却是在前臂中间位置弯曲，这感觉真的很奇怪。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:49.29,1:01:50.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I was like, uh, I was so ashamed.\N我当时觉得特别羞愧。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:50.81,1:01:51.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm like, we're gonna get this thing out.\N我心想，我们得把这个东西弄出去。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.92,1:01:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like, you know, at the time I was like, this is incredible.\N当时我觉得，这简直太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:54.72,1:01:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did you sell any of these?\N你把这些东西卖出去了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.68,1:01:56.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,We didn't sell them.\N我们没卖过。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.28,1:01:57.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just used them internally.\N只是内部自己用了。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:57.42,1:02:00.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we showed it and it was like this big like forearm.\N但我们展示过，它看起来就像个特别大的前臂。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:00.22,1:02:02.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was like, "Everybody's going to notice this big forearm.\N我心想，所有人都会注意到这个大大的前臂。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:02.23,1:02:03.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to be so weird."\N这也太奇怪了。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:03.20,1:02:03.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:03.52,1:02:09.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I don't think I've ever had a single person in like three years ask why the form looks like this.\N而且我觉得过去三年里，从来没有人问过我为什么这个造型是这样的。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:09.36,1:02:09.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really?\N真的吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:02:09.87,1:02:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone was like, "It's a robot."\N大家都说是机器人。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:12.08,1:02:13.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not a single one.\N一个都没有。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:13.56,1:02:14.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:14.05,1:02:20.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we uh so we end up pivoting away from like the tendon driven hand to our current generations of hands.\N所以我们最终转向了现在的手部设计，不再使用肌腱驱动的手。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:20.71,1:02:28.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um I we we've learned a lot, but like I um yeah, we ultimately I think are building like some of the best hand technology in the world.\N我们学到了很多，但我觉得我们最终正在打造世界上顶尖的手部技术之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:28.39,1:02:36.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We recently unveiled our um high degree of freedom uh hand as a teaser, our next generation hand uh about a month ago.\N我们最近发布了一个预告，展示了我们下一代高自由度的手，大约一个月前。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:37.00,1:02:44.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,This hand has uh basically a human level dexterity like as many joints in the hand as a human.\N这只手基本上具备人类水平的灵巧性，关节数量和人类的手一样多。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:44.50,1:02:50.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and this is really important not just for like being able to dextrous tasks, but we need to be able to learn passively from humans at scale.\N这点非常重要，不仅是因为能完成精细操作，还因为我们需要能大规模地从人类行为中被动学习。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:50.32,1:02:56.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh, if humans can move hands in all these different crazy way, we we need to be able to map to this uh, at test time on the robot.\N如果人类能以各种奇怪的方式移动手，我们就必须能在机器人测试时映射出这些动作。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:56.63,1:03:01.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we have um, I think this is extremely important to get if we want to solve like uh, uh,\N所以，我认为这一点非常重要，如果我们想解决类似……
Dialogue: 0,1:03:01.43,1:03:07.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,AGI and get to like human intelligence in the physical world, like it's all going to start here with the hands for us.\N通用人工智能，并实现物理世界中的人类智能，对我们来说，一切都将从双手开始。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:07.28,1:03:08.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's intense.\N是的，这很激烈。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:08.68,1:03:09.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's complex.\N这很复杂。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:09.66,1:03:15.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I did see a couple people walking around the campus in spandex outfits.\N我确实看到有几个员工在校园里穿着紧身衣走来走去。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:15.20,1:03:19.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's a mandatory outfit at work.\N是的，这是工作时的强制着装。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.52,1:03:22.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, like you just got to be in spandex so you can't come.\N是的，你必须穿紧身衣，不然就别来上班。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:22.87,1:03:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um yeah so we basically are doing a lot of data collection here where we're trying to I basically do like joint level tracking uh and\N嗯，是的，我们基本上在这里做了大量数据收集，主要是进行关节级追踪，还有
Dialogue: 0,1:03:29.68,1:03:35.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,different type of uh data collection efforts like learning from humans like our our training set is like how do we like we're a humanoid like we\N各种类型的数据收集工作，比如从人类身上学习，我们的训练数据集就是如何像人类一样，我们是人形机器人，
Dialogue: 0,1:03:35.68,1:03:38.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,need to learn from humans at scale and so we're trying to learn\N所以我们必须大规模地向人类学习，因此我们正努力学习
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.46,1:03:43.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,as much as possible about human movements and like image conditioning these policies uh\N尽可能多的人类运动数据，以及图像条件下的策略。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:43.68,1:03:52.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,here at figure is that the oddest job um what is that called um what is the oddest job in the office is you think That's odd.\N在这里做这份工作，感觉是最奇怪的，呃，这工作叫什么来着，呃，\N办公室里最奇怪的工作是什么？你觉得这很奇怪。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:52.65,1:03:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's kind of cool.\N我觉得这挺酷的。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:53.68,1:03:54.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's uncommon.\N这很不寻常。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:54.56,1:03:57.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's uncommon.\N是啊，很不寻常。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.25,1:03:59.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, probably the oddest job we have there.\N嗯，可能是我们那里最奇怪的工作了。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.76,1:04:00.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是啊。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:00.72,1:04:02.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,How does one apply?\N那该怎么申请呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:04:02.16,1:04:03.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,You apply on the site.\N你可以在网站上申请。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:03.26,1:04:04.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,You apply on the website.\N你可以在官网上申请。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.55,1:04:04.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.75,1:04:08.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,we do like we basically have like data collection folks that we basically are here\N我们基本上有专门负责数据收集的人员，他们既在这里，也在世界各地为 Helix 收集数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:08.90,1:04:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we have both here and out in the world doing data collection for Helix.\N我们既有在这里的，也有在世界各地为 Helix 进行数据收集的人员。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:12.24,1:04:12.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's cool.\N这挺酷的。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:12.80,1:04:13.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.16,1:04:13.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.52,1:04:13.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.88,1:04:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's I actually think it's a really cool job.\N我 actually 觉得这是一份非常酷的工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:15.92,1:04:16.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have you ever tried it?\N你试过吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:04:16.72,1:04:17.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, full spandex.\N嗯，全贴身紧身衣。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:17.63,1:04:17.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:17.93,1:04:21.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, I haven't tried the full spandex, but I've done every other type of data collection effort here.\N嗯，我还没试过全贴身紧身衣，但这里其他类型的数据采集工作我都做过。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:21.68,1:04:22.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe that'll be your next job.\N也许那会是你的下一个工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:22.96,1:04:23.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe we should.\N也许我们应该试试。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:23.48,1:04:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'm going to go get in some spandex later and I'll test it out.\N嗯，我待会儿要去穿件紧身衣试试看。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:27.52,1:04:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so we saw the generation of hands.\N好的，我们看到了手部的生成过程。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:30.00,1:04:31.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so generation hands.\N好的，这是机械手部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:31.60,1:04:34.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, we also have some um some mockups for the head and feet.\N嗯，我们还为头部和脚部做了一些原型模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:34.74,1:04:36.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the feet are actually really interesting here.\N我觉得脚部在这里其实非常有趣。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:36.78,1:04:38.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, this is kind of our first prototype for Figure 03.\N嗯，这基本上是我们 Figure 03 的第一个原型。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:39.02,1:04:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, it's like basically like we really wanted to get a toe in the robot,\N嗯，我们主要是想让机器人真正具备脚趾功能，
Dialogue: 0,1:04:43.52,1:04:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is important both for like a natural looking gate like as you walk, but also like getting off off the ground.\N这对实现自然的步态——比如走路时——以及离地动作都很重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.32,1:04:48.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.64,1:04:49.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is really important.\N这真的很重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:49.41,1:04:50.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or even squatting down.\N甚至包括下蹲动作。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:50.31,1:04:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we squat down, we're like on our toe box.\N当我们下蹲时，身体是靠脚趾前端支撑的。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:52.56,1:04:54.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and it's really difficult with a flat foot.\N而用平脚掌则非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:54.80,1:04:58.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and then basically this is our this is our Figure 02 like foot.\N嗯，然后这基本上就是我们 Figure 02 的脚部设计。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:58.21,1:05:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's basically just a a fixed piece of metal.\N基本上就是一块固定的金属。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:01.36,1:05:03.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, nothing too crazy impressive.\N嗯，没什么特别惊人或令人印象深刻的地方。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.94,1:05:08.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then this is our current generation of feet is for Figure 03.\N然后这是我们现在为 Figure 03 开发的脚部设计。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:08.88,1:05:10.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,We basically have a toe.\N我们基本上有一个脚趾。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:10.56,1:05:13.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have this um opening here in the foot.\N脚部这里有个开口。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:13.30,1:05:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um some people ask about this.\N有些人会问起这个。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:15.04,1:05:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is basically for like thermal venting as we're charging.\N这主要是为了在充电时散热。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:18.64,1:05:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're pushing air through the calf and the shin uh through through the foot\N我们通过小腿和小腿前部，再经过脚部，将空气吹进去，
Dialogue: 0,1:05:22.16,1:05:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,to cool it down as it's charging because it's got inductive coils on the bottom.\N以在充电时降温，因为底部装有感应线圈。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:26.24,1:05:31.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So these feet are basically uh basically stepping onto uh this basically the charger.\N所以这些脚基本上是踩在充电器上。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:31.21,1:05:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we we then initiate charge like a wirelessly and the the robot can charge at two kilowatts.\N然后我们通过无线方式启动充电，机器人可以以两千瓦的功率充电。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:36.80,1:05:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So basically we can charge for an hour by standing there.\N所以基本上，只要站那儿一小时，就能完成充电。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:40.32,1:05:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's really cool.\N这真的很酷。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:41.28,1:05:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's really cool.\N这真的很酷。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.00,1:05:42.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.24,1:05:44.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can charge like at client sites like this.\N我们可以在客户现场像这样充电。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:44.51,1:05:47.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can walk over uh we can dock to it.\N我们可以走过去，然后把它对接上。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:47.38,1:05:49.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can just stand on it.\N我们可以直接站上去。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.08,1:05:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um over time we're going to get these uh systems uh even smaller and uh be able to put\N随着时间推移，我们会让这些系统变得更小，基本上可以放到任何地方。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:54.52,1:05:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,them basically be able to put it anywhere and you can plug this into a normal wall outlet for charging.\N你可以把它插到普通墙插上充电。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:58.88,1:06:00.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you going to do any brand deals?\N你会做品牌合作吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:00.88,1:06:02.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um like foot brand like foot deals.\N比如鞋类品牌的合作？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:02.78,1:06:05.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I would love to do maybe not foot but sneaker deals.\N我倒是想做，不过可能不是鞋类，而是运动鞋的合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:05.44,1:06:09.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sneaker deals if like if Nikey's watching like be our next uh Yeah.\N如果运动鞋品牌在看的话，比如耐克，就来成为我们的下一个合作方吧，行吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:09.07,1:06:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nike sneaker shoe dealer.\N耐克运动鞋经销商。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.32,1:06:10.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.66,1:06:12.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,I really wanted a high top for Figure 03.\N我真的很想要一双高帮鞋给 Figure 03。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:12.85,1:06:13.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's just like so cool.\N我觉得这简直太酷了。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:13.92,1:06:14.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.08,1:06:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's pretty cool.\N确实很酷。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.56,1:06:18.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um like our Figure 02 looks like a like a penny loafer and just like you know what I mean?\N嗯，就像我们的 Figure 02 看起来像一双便士乐福鞋，你懂我的意思吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:18.08,1:06:18.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can't be having that.\N这可不行。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:18.89,1:06:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. We can't have a penny loafer out here.\N不，我们不能让一双便士乐福鞋出现在这里。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:20.24,1:06:22.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like this high top's like kind of made to doing work.\N这双高帮鞋看起来就是为工作设计的。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:22.56,1:06:26.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,So of the designs here like you have quite a sleek design.\N所以这些设计里，你有相当简洁的造型。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:26.41,1:06:28.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's very futuristic.\N非常具有未来感。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:28.23,1:06:32.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,How did how did like how did you get to this point?\N你是怎么走到这一步的？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:32.40,1:06:32.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,\N是的，
Dialogue: 0,1:06:32.72,1:06:39.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have a design we have a industrial design team here internally run by uh David uh who you just met and we we have a team that\N我们有一个设计，这里有一个工业设计团队，由你刚见到的戴维负责，我们还有一个团队，
Dialogue: 0,1:06:39.88,1:06:50.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,are obsessed with trying to create like uh yeah trying to create like the um we we want to create something that uh is really delightful to be around.\N他们痴迷于打造一种……是的，我们想创造一种……真正让人感到愉悦的体验。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.61,1:06:55.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um it's it's not just like the way the robot looks or the size of it.\N这不仅仅关乎机器人的外观或大小。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:55.32,1:07:00.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's how it walks and interacts and how it's body language and how the human machine interaction.\N还在于它走路的方式、互动方式、肢体语言以及人机交互的体验。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:00.41,1:07:02.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it does it look at you while it's while it's talking?\N它说话的时候会看着你吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:02.79,1:07:04.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh how do we deal with speech?\N那我们该如何处理语音？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:04.40,1:07:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do we do with like we have like three screens in the head?\N我们头上有三块屏幕，那该显示什么内容？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:06.72,1:07:07.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what do we show there?\N比如说，我们该在上面展示什么？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:07.66,1:07:10.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do they make us like really pleasant to be around?\N它们如何让我们感觉真正舒适、愉悦？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:10.48,1:07:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are there any I mean you love sci-fi.\N你不是喜欢科幻吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:12.64,1:07:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Were there any sci-fi movies where you wanted Oh yeah, like the robot movies.\N有哪部科幻电影让你特别想参与吗？嗯，比如机器人题材的电影。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:16.16,1:07:17.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I, Robot. Ex Machina.\N《我，机器人》和《机械姬》。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:17.60,1:07:18.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like which ones?\N比如哪些电影？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:19.04,1:07:22.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think a thing we always talk about here is like there's like two roads for humanoids.\N我觉得我们一直讨论的一个问题是，人形机器人有两条发展路径。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:22.28,1:07:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's like a road to head like down like the robotic road which is like I robot and there's a road to head down for like Westworld.\N一条是走向机器人之路，就像《我，机器人》那样，另一条是走向类似《西部世界》的路径。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:28.00,1:07:28.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:28.32,1:07:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's also humanoid.\N它也是人形机器人。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:29.28,1:07:29.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:29.68,1:07:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh where do we go?\N那我们接下来该往哪儿走？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:32.32,1:07:34.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you think?\N你觉得呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:34.08,1:07:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean I'm a big fan of XM.\N嗯，我其实很推崇 XM。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.28,1:07:37.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.64,1:07:38.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we go to Westworld.\N所以我们去西部世界。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:39.04,1:07:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:39.52,1:07:39.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:39.98,1:07:40.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:40.44,1:07:41.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's do it.\N我们开始吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:41.44,1:07:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:42.24,1:07:45.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're heading to Westworld.\N我们正前往西部世界。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:46.00,1:07:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think lastly is we're like super proud to be on the cover of Time magazine this past year which is really cool.\N嗯，我觉得最后一点是，我们非常自豪今年登上了《时代》杂志封面，这真的很酷。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:51.32,1:07:55.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we had a robot in in uh in a home basically doing like full\N嗯，我们有个机器人，基本上在一家人家中，像这样
Dialogue: 0,1:07:55.60,1:08:01.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,like you know like doing housework with Helix um AI system that we designed here internally.\N完全使用我们内部设计的 Helix AI 系统来完成家务。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:01.20,1:08:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um what's with the Deadmau5 record?\NDeadmau5 的那张唱片是怎么回事？
Dialogue: 0,1:08:04.08,1:08:10.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah we had uh we had Deadmau5 at our holiday party two years ago and he was like this is insane.\N哦对，两年前我们年会请了 Deadmau5，他当时说这太疯狂了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:10.95,1:08:16.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had robots on stage like I got to get you guys out to concerts with me and we got to be like dancing on stage.\N我们让机器人登台了，就像我要带你们去我的演唱会，还要在台上一起跳舞。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:16.27,1:08:16.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:16.56,1:08:20.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we opened for him at Red Rock uh end of last year uh in Colorado.\N所以我们去年年底在科罗拉多州的红岩为他开业了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:20.41,1:08:22.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know if you've been to the uh concert.\N我不知道你有没有去过那个音乐会。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:22.72,1:08:23.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,I flew in for it.\N我专程飞来参加。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:23.42,1:08:23.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was amazing.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.04,1:08:28.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just like amazing venue and we had multiple robots on stage just dancing and they're all tuned in\N就像令人惊叹的场地一样，我们让多台机器人上台跳舞，它们全都调谐到位了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:28.85,1:08:33.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the music and um and they kind of danced with it and it was just it was awesome.\N随着音乐，他们仿佛与音乐共舞，真是太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:33.10,1:08:36.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we had him also here at our last holiday party in December.\N而且我们去年12月的假日派对上也把他带来了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:36.14,1:08:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh I don't know just we just we just raged with Deadmau5.\N呃，我不太知道，反正我们就是跟 Deadmau5 一起嗨翻了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.08,1:08:40.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey, it's Molly.\N嗨，我是莫莉。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.94,1:08:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you enjoy our interviews,\N如果你喜欢我们的采访，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.32,1:08:51.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,check out our newsletter sourcery.vc where we deliver a once a week top deals and tech headlines email and also go deeper on our podcast interviews.\N了解我们的新闻简报 Sourcery.vc，\N每周为您推送精选交易和科技头条，还可深入收听我们的播客访谈。
